  <page>
    <title>Olivia, Minnesota</title>
    <id>121550</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40624262</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-21T22:26:46Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>216.16.79.97</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* External links */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Olivia''' is a city located in [[Renville County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,570.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Renville County, Minnesota|Renville County]][[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt;]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Olivia.png|right|Location of Olivia, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 6.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.0 km&amp;sup2; (2.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 2,570 people, 1,075 households, and 658 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 425.9/km&amp;sup2; (1,102.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,178 housing units at an average density of 195.2/km&amp;sup2; (505.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.19% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.12% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.12% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.12% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.57% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.89% from two or more races.  7.63% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,075 households out of which 28.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 52.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 38.7% are non-families. 35.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 18.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.30 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.7% under the age of 18, 7.2% from 18 to 24, 23.5% from 25 to 44, 22.8% from 45 to 64, and 21.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $35,060, and the median income for a family is $44,781. Males have a median income of $31,793 versus $25,541 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,889.  11.3% of the population and 6.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 17.2% of those under the age of 18 and 10.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Corn Capital of the World ==

The [[Minnesota Senate]] has designated Olivia the &quot;[[Maize|Corn]] Capital of the World&quot;. Olivia has been calling itself the &quot;Corn Capital of the World&quot; since 1973, when it erected its well-known 50-foot corn monument in the shape of an ear of corn.  Olivia is the home to nine seed research facilities of its own. It's located in the middle of [[Renville County]], Minnesota's leading producer of corn.

[[Constantine, Michigan]] is the &quot;Seed Corn Capital of the World.&quot;

== City-Wide Celebrations ==
Olivia celebrates '''Corn Capital Days''' during the last weekend of July.  Activities include a parade, corn cob toss, corn-lympics, free corn feed, kiddie parade, Lion's Walk-in, Fly-in, Drive-in breakfast, and live music (2005 music featured [[Kory and the Fireflies]], [[Ripchord]], and [[Down and Above]]).

== External links ==
*[http://www.olivia.mn.us/ Olivia official website]
*[http://www.oliviahomes.com/ Homes in Olivia, Minnesota]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:Renville County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Olivia, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
