      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Richland Township''' is a township located in [[Rice County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 471.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 93.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (36.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  93.4 km&amp;sup2; (36.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 471 people, 162 households, and 131 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 5.0/km&amp;sup2; (13.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 166 housing units at an average density of 1.8/km&amp;sup2; (4.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 99.58% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.42% from two or more races.  1.49% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 162 households out of which 37.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 74.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 1.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 19.1% are non-families. 16.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.91 and the average family size is 3.28.

In the township the population is spread out with 28.5% under the age of 18, 6.2% from 18 to 24, 32.9% from 25 to 44, 21.4% from 45 to 64, and 11.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 107.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 116.0 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $59,911, and the median income for a family is $63,375. Males have a median income of $35,809 versus $29,250 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $18,956.  2.7% of the population and 0.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 0.0% of those under the age of 18 and 12.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

[[Category:Rice County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Townships in Minnesota]]</text>
