      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wheeling Township''' is a township located in [[Rice County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 541.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 89.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (34.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  89.7 km&amp;sup2; (34.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of its area is water.

The southern half of the township is flat, and land use is agricultural.  The northern half is made up of rolling hills, and land use is predominantly rural and residential.

Prairie Creek is the most prominent drainage system.  The entire township is part of the [[Cannon River]] watershed.

The Nerstrand-Big Woods state park is located in Wheeling township.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 541 people, 176 households, and 145 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 6.0/km&amp;sup2; (15.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 178 housing units at an average density of 2.0/km&amp;sup2; (5.1/mi&amp;sup2;).

The racial makeup of the township is 98.89% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.37% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.37% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.18% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.18% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

The northernmost portion of the township was originally settled by [[Norwegian-American|Norwegian]] immigrants, while the balance was originally settled by [[German-American|German]] immigrants.  Much of the land is still farmed by families whose ancestors settled the area in the late 19th century. Main Street in [[Nerstrand, Minnesota]], extended westward, formed the dividing line.

There are 176 households out of which 47.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 72.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 2.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 17.6% are non-families. 13.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.06 and the average family size is 3.41.

In the township the population is spread out with 32.5% under the age of 18, 7.4% from 18 to 24, 34.0% from 25 to 44, 19.0% from 45 to 64, and 7.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 104.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 116.0 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $48,056, and the median income for a family is $49,583. Males have a median income of $33,462 versus $30,000 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $17,944.  5.7% of the population and 4.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 7.2% of those under the age of 18 and 5.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

[[Category:Rice County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Townships in Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
