== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 3,789 people, 1,396 households, and 949 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 360.3/km&amp;sup2; (932.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,424 housing units at an average density of 135.4/km&amp;sup2; (350.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.39% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.13% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.40% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.71% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.45% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.92% from two or more races.  1.13% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,396 households out of which 38.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 53.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.0% are non-families. 26.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.59 and the average family size is 3.13.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.1% under the age of 18, 7.3% from 18 to 24, 31.3% from 25 to 44, 17.1% from 45 to 64, and 16.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 97.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $50,272, and the median income for a family is $59,539. Males have a median income of $39,292 versus $27,054 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $19,433.  5.8% of the population and 2.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 6.3% of those under the age of 18 and 14.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.


== Education ==

The Belle Plaine Public Schools service nearly 1,400 students in grades Kindergarten through 12th grade. The district is growing at approximately 4% per year.

== History ==

Minnesota Territorial Judge Andrew G. Chatfield selected this townsite in 1853 while traveling on horseback from Mendota to Traverse des Sioux to hold court. Judge Chatfield chose to name the townsite Belle Plaine, French for &quot;beautiful prairie.&quot;

=== Administration (2004)===
Kelly D. Smith, Ed.D., Superintendent (ksmith@belleplaine.k12.mn.us)&lt;br&gt;
Mr. Lowell Hoffman, High School Principal (lhoffman@belleplaine.k12.mn.us)&lt;br&gt;
Mr. John Miller, Jr. High Principal/District Curriculum Coordinator(jmiller@belleplaine.k12.mn.us)&lt;br&gt;
Ms. JoAnne Tierney, Elementary Principal (jtierney@belleplaine.k12.mn.us)&lt;br&gt;

Web site: http://www.belleplaine.k12.mn.us
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:Scott County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Belle Plaine, Minnesota]]</text>
