In the township the population is spread out with 30.1% under the age of 18, 6.5% from 18 to 24, 29.7% from 25 to 44, 21.8% from 45 to 64, and 11.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 114.1 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $51,000, and the median income for a family is $53,462. Males have a median income of $36,793 versus $29,375 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $18,621.  5.3% of the population and 5.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 5.4% of those under the age of 18 and 8.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
