      <text xml:space="preserve">'''New Market Township''' is a township located in [[Scott County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 3,057.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 87.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (33.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  87.5 km&amp;sup2; (33.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.21% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 3,057 people, 956 households, and 834 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 35.0/km&amp;sup2; (90.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 976 housing units at an average density of 11.2/km&amp;sup2; (28.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.23% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.20% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.23% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.23% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.49% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.59% from two or more races.  1.08% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 956 households out of which 48.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 81.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 3.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 12.7% are non-families. 8.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 2.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.20 and the average family size is 3.39.

In the township the population is spread out with 33.2% under the age of 18, 5.0% from 18 to 24, 33.4% from 25 to 44, 24.4% from 45 to 64, and 4.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 109.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 102.3 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $82,718, and the median income for a family is $85,880. Males have a median income of $50,811 versus $32,639 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $31,176.  2.3% of the population and 0.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 1.4% of those under the age of 18 and 5.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
