      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;!-- Unsourced image removed: [[Image:Priorlake air.jpg|thumb|Aerial photo of Prior Lake looking northeast. Upper Prior Lake is in the foreground, Lower Prior Lake is in the back.]] --&gt;'''Prior Lake''' is a city located in [[Scott County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 15,917.  The [[Shakopee-Mdewakanton Indian Reservation]] lies within the city.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Prior_Lake.png|right|Location of Prior Lake, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 41.5 [[square kilometer|km²]] (16.0 [[square mile|mi²]]).  35.0 km² (13.5 mi²) of it is land and 6.6 km² (2.5 mi²) of it is water.  The total area is 15.77% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 15,917 people, 5,645 households, and 4,386 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 454.9/km² (1,178.4/mi²).  There are 5,791 housing units at an average density of 165.5/km² (428.7/mi²).  The racial makeup of the city is 94.53% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.77% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 2.08% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.94% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.33% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.31% from two or more races.  1.11% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,645 households out of which 44.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 66.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 22.3% are non-families. 15.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.82 and the average family size is 3.17.

In the city the population is spread out with 30.3% under the age of 18, 6.4% from 18 to 24, 37.7% from 25 to 44, 20.7% from 45 to 64, and 4.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 102.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 102.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $75,363, and the median income for a family is $81,011. Males have a median income of $52,061 versus $34,837 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $32,089.  3.6% of the population and 1.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 3.4% of those under the age of 18 and 7.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Local Issues ==

The [http://www.cityofpriorlake.com City of Prior Lake] contains a lake after the same name that is divided into Upper Prior Lake and Lower Prior Lake. Prior Lake is the largest lake south of the river [[Minneapolis-St. Paul]] [[metropolitan area]] and the city is generally considered to be an [[exurb]] of Minneapolis St. Paul. 

The lake attracts large [[beach homes]] that increases the wealth of the surrounding area. Add this with [[Mystic Lake Casino]] which is on the [[Shakopee-Mdewakanton Indian Reservation]] and operated by the Shakopee Mdewakanton Sioux Community, Prior Lake is one of the wealthier cities in Minnesota. As a result the students of Prior Lake High School have gained a notoriety for prevalent drug and alcohol abuse. 

''The'' [http://www.plamerican.com ''Prior Lake American''], the city newspaper, is one of the best sources of information in the city. Others include This Week Prior Lake and the Star Tribune South Edition.

After the 1999 shootings at [[Columbine High School]], author Elinor Burkett wrote a book, [http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/0060505850 Another Planet], detailing her experience following several students around for one school year at Prior Lake High School. 

As of July 1, 2004, the city's population was estimated at 21,286, and is projected to grow to 42,400 by build-out in 2030. To guide the future of the community, stakeholders from across the community spectrum have come together to create and update a long-term vision for the city's future, the 2030 Vision and Strategic Plan. Created by the community and for the community, this document [http://www.cityofpriorlake.com City of Prior Lake] is the driving force behind all the positive things that are happening in Prior Lake!  But don't take our word for it. See for yourself why Prior Lake is such a wonderful place to call home.

== Politics ==
Prior Lake is in the 2nd [[Congressional District]] of Minnesota represented by Congressman [[John Kline (politician)|John Kline]], a Republican first elected in 2002.
Prior Lake is in the Minnesota Legislative District 35A.  The district 35 Senator is [[Claire Robling]] (R).  The district 35A Representative is [[Michael Beard]] (R)

[[Category:Scott County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[io:Prior Lake, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
