        <ip>24.123.127.98</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Shakopee''' is a city located in [[Scott County, Minnesota]]. As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 20,568.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Scott County, Minnesota|Scott County]][[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt;]]. The [[Valleyfair]] [[amusement park]] and the [[Canterbury Park]] [[horse]] racetrack are located in Shakopee, as is the site of the [[Minnesota]] [[Renaissance fair|Renaissance Festival]] (Ren-Fest).

Records indicate that a Dakota Indian village was located east of the present day city of Shakopee. The village was called Teen-tah-o-tan-wa, “village of the prairie”, and was the home of summer bark lodges, winter tipis and cornfields. The Minnesota River acted as a natural and beautiful boundary from the Ojibway to the north. The tribal leader of Teenatahotonwa was Chief Shakopee (pronounced Shah-kpa-dan or Shakpay). He was the leader for which the City of Shakopee is named. The burial mounds near the Minnesota River are a reminder of Chief Shakopee’s village and the rich heritage and tradition of the city’s original inhabitants. They are estimated to be over 2,000 years old.

== Education ==
Shakopee is home to four elementary schools, one junior high school and one senior high school. The elementary schools are [[Pearson Elementary]], [[Red Oak Elementary]], [[Sun Path Elementary]], and [[Sweeney Elementary]]. The Junior High School is called [[Shakopee Junior High ]] School while the Senior High School is called [[Shakopee Senior High School]]. A construction project is underway to build a new high school due to the influx of more students.

Shakopee is also the home of the [http://www.sacsschools.org/ Shakopee Area Catholic Schools].

Recently, A Shakopee Junior High School Gym teacher was accused of having sexual relations with a student. The teacher admitted to having a sexual relationship with the 15 year old female student, who willingly went to the teacher's house. The female student tried to break off the relationship but the teacher threatened suicide. The teacher is due in court some time in January.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Shakopee.png|right|Location of Shakopee, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 73.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (28.5 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  69.9 km&amp;sup2; (27.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 3.8 km&amp;sup2; (1.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 5.10% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 20,568 people, 7,540 households, and 5,360 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 294.1/km&amp;sup2; (761.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 7,805 housing units at an average density of 111.6/km&amp;sup2; (289.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 91.61% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.33% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.94% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 2.41% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.14% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.54% from two or more races.  4.40% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 7,540 households out of which 38.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 58.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.9% are non-families. 21.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.66 and the average family size is 3.12.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.5% under the age of 18, 8.9% from 18 to 24, 38.8% from 25 to 44, 17.5% from 45 to 64, and 7.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 98.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 94.6 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $59,137, and the median income for a family is $66,885. Males have a median income of $41,662 versus $32,244 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $25,128.  3.5% of the population and 1.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 3.6% of those under the age of 18 and 4.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==References==
* [http://wcco.com/crime/local_story_339104851.html][Teacher Accused Of Sexual Relations With Student]

[[Category:Scott County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[io:Shakopee, Minnesota]]

[http://www.ci.shakopee.mn.us/ City of Shakopee Website]</text>
    </revision>
