  <page>
    <title>Elk River, Minnesota</title>
    <id>121667</id>
    <revision>
      <id>30291137</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-06T01:55:48Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>68.112.131.178</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Elk River''' is a city located in [[Sherburne County, Minnesota]], about 34 miles northwest of [[Minneapolis, Minnesota|Minneapolis]]. It is situated at the confluence of the [[Mississippi River|Mississippi]] and [[Elk River (Minnesota)|Elk]] Rivers.  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 16,447.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Sherburne County, Minnesota|Sherburne County]][[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt;]]. According to [[city data]], Elk River's population has finally reached the 20,000 person mark as of 2004.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Elk_River.png|right|Location of Elk River, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 113.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (43.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  110.5 km&amp;sup2; (42.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 3.0 km&amp;sup2; (1.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.67% water. The city's [[latitude]] and [[longitude]] are 45.313601° N and 93.5814° W.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 16,447 people, 5,664 households, and 4,400 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 148.9/km&amp;sup2; (385.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 5,782 housing units at an average density of 52.3/km&amp;sup2; (135.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.18% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.44% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.37% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.49% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.48% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.02% from two or more races.  1.33% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,664 households out of which 45.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 64.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 22.3% are non-families. 17.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.85 and the average family size is 3.24.

In the city the population is spread out with 31.3% under the age of 18, 8.5% from 18 to 24, 33.9% from 25 to 44, 18.3% from 45 to 64, and 8.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 100.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $58,114, and the median income for a family is $65,471. Males have a median income of $43,230 versus $30,023 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $21,808.  3.2% of the population and 2.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.9% of those under the age of 18 and 4.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Transportation ==
The city of Elk River is a busy city when it comes to traffic. Major highways include [[MN-101]] which ends at the crossroads of [[US-169]] and [[US-10]]. There is an on-demand bus service available to its' citizens, which is called 'RiverRider.' There is also a bus service between [[Elk River]], [[Coon Rapids]], and [[Minneapolis]], called the [[NorthStar Commuter Coach]]. Fares for that are $4.50 from Elk River and $2.75 from Coon Rapids to Minneapolis, and the opposite on the way back.
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:Sherburne County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities on the Mississippi River]]

[[io:Elk River, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
