      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Santiago Township''' is a township located in [[Sherburne County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 1,555.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 94.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (36.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  93.5 km&amp;sup2; (36.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.6 km&amp;sup2; (0.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.63% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,555 people, 477 households, and 395 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 16.6/km&amp;sup2; (43.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 483 housing units at an average density of 5.2/km&amp;sup2; (13.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.39% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.26% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.19% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.13% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.06% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.96% from two or more races.  0.26% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 477 households out of which 53.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 74.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 3.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 17.0% are non-families. 12.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.18 and the average family size is 3.46.

In the township the population is spread out with 35.0% under the age of 18, 6.4% from 18 to 24, 37.4% from 25 to 44, 16.0% from 45 to 64, and 5.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 31 years.  For every 100 females there are 108.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 113.5 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $58,688, and the median income for a family is $60,962. Males have a median income of $40,982 versus $26,587 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $19,029.  8.5% of the population and 5.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.4% of those under the age of 18 and 13.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

