      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For other things named &quot;Zimmerman&quot;, see [[Zimmerman (disambiguation)]]''


'''Zimmerman''' is a city located in [[Sherburne County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,851.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Zimmerman.png|right|Location of Zimmerman, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 7.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  7.2 km&amp;sup2; (2.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.80% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 2,851 people, 963 households, and 722 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 396.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,026.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,018 housing units at an average density of 141.4/km&amp;sup2; (366.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.61% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.11% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.25% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.28% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.35% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.40% from two or more races.  1.30% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 963 households out of which 49.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 56.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.0% are non-families. 17.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.96 and the average family size is 3.39.

In the city the population is spread out with 36.0% under the age of 18, 9.2% from 18 to 24, 37.0% from 25 to 44, 13.2% from 45 to 64, and 4.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 27 years.  For every 100 females there are 99.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.7 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $49,332, and the median income for a family is $51,275. Males have a median income of $37,298 versus $24,918 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,528.  6.3% of the population and 4.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 8.2% of those under the age of 18 and 17.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

[[Category:Sherburne County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

