      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Faxon Township''' is a township located in [[Sibley County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 598.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 55.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (21.5 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  54.3 km&amp;sup2; (21.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.33% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 598 people, 188 households, and 156 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 11.0/km&amp;sup2; (28.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 193 housing units at an average density of 3.6/km&amp;sup2; (9.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.33% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.17% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.50% from two or more races.  1.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

