      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Gibbon''' is a city located in [[Sibley County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 808.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Gibbon.png|right|Location of Gibbon, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.  The [[Rush River (Minnesota)|Middle Branch Rush River]] starts near Gaylord.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 808 people, 364 households, and 227 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 350.5/km&amp;sup2; (910.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 378 housing units at an average density of 164.0/km&amp;sup2; (425.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 95.17% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.74% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.50% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.09% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.50% from two or more races.  3.84% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 364 households out of which 25.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 5.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 37.6% are non-families. 34.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 20.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.22 and the average family size is 2.88.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.3% under the age of 18, 5.9% from 18 to 24, 23.5% from 25 to 44, 19.4% from 45 to 64, and 26.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 103.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 102.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $33,816, and the median income for a family is $38,977. Males have a median income of $30,625 versus $22,019 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,897.  7.4% of the population and 3.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.7% of those under the age of 18 and 8.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
