      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Winthrop''' is a city located in [[Sibley County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,367.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Winthrop.png|right|Location of Winthrop, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.7 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.  The [[Rush River (Minnesota)|South Branch Rush River]] starts near Winthrop.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,367 people, 591 households, and 346 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 502.7/km&amp;sup2; (1,303.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 632 housing units at an average density of 232.4/km&amp;sup2; (602.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 93.71% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.07% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.29% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.15% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 4.54% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.24% from two or more races.  6.95% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 591 households out of which 26.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 41.3% are non-families. 38.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.22 and the average family size is 2.96.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.7% under the age of 18, 6.1% from 18 to 24, 23.3% from 25 to 44, 21.2% from 45 to 64, and 25.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 83.6 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $34,813, and the median income for a family is $47,159. Males have a median income of $31,149 versus $20,573 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,188.  6.1% of the population and 3.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 5.7% of those under the age of 18 and 8.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

