      <comment>/* Geography */ map</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Aurora''' is a city located in [[St. Louis County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,850.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Aurora.png|right|Location of Aurora, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 10.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9.8 km&amp;sup2; (3.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.4 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 3.56% water.  It is surrounded by mixed coniferous/deciduous forest and is near man lakes.

== Economy == 
Aurora is located on the [[Mesabi Range]] of northeastern Minnesota.  Formerly this area produced a large quanitity of the nation's [[iron]] and [[taconite]] ore, but recently they have been depleted or become too expensive to mine.  Recently a Blue Cross Blue Shield call center has been built in Aurora, and it is hoped that more jobs will come to the area.

== Recreation ==
Aurora is located on the edge of the [[Superior National Forest]], and is located two miles from Giants Ridge Golf &amp; Ski Resort.  Popular recreational activities of the residents of Aurora and nearby area include hunting, [[fishing]], boating, four-wheeling, [[skiing]], and [[snowboarding]].  There are many [[all-terrain vehicle|ATV]] and [[snowmobile]] trails on the outskirts of Aurora, and many of these go far, some all the way to [[Lake Superior]].

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,850 people, 812 households, and 495 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 188.0/km&amp;sup2; (487.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 893 housing units at an average density of 90.7/km&amp;sup2; (235.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 98.38% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.05% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.43% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.38% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.05% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.70% from two or more races.  0.32% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 812 households out of which 22.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 39.0% are non-families. 34.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.19 and the average family size is 2.79.

In the city the population is spread out with 19.8% under the age of 18, 7.2% from 18 to 24, 22.6% from 25 to 44, 26.4% from 45 to 64, and 23.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 45 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $32,094, and the median income for a family is $43,095. Males have a median income of $41,413 versus $20,625 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,442.  11.9% of the population and 8.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 26.0% of those under the age of 18 and 4.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:St. Louis County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Aurora, Minnesota]]</text>
