      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Ely''' is a city located in [[St. Louis County, Minnesota]], [[United States]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,724. The city is best known by outsiders as the most popular entry point for the [[Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Ely.png|right|Location of Ely, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 7.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  7.0 km&amp;sup2; (2.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 3,724 people, 1,694 households, and 916 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 528.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,369.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,912 housing units at an average density of 271.4/km&amp;sup2; (703.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.86% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.86% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.54% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.19% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.30% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.26% from two or more races.  0.67% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,694 households out of which 21.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 41.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 45.9% are non-families. 39.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.05 and the average family size is 2.72.

In the city the population is spread out with 17.8% under the age of 18, 16.2% from 18 to 24, 21.6% from 25 to 44, 22.9% from 45 to 64, and 21.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 102.6 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $27,615, and the median income for a family is $36,047. Males have a median income of $34,559 versus $18,833 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,855.  14.5% of the population and 9.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.9% of those under the age of 18 and 12.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Notable residents==
* Jim Brandenberg
* [[Sigurd F. Olson]]
* [[Will Steger]]

