      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Embarrass Township''' is a township located in [[St. Louis County, Minnesota]], [[United States]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 691. In January 2005 Embarrass had a record low temperature of –54°F.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 84.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (32.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  84.7 km&amp;sup2; (32.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.24% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 691 people, 290 households, and 196 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 8.2/km&amp;sup2; (21.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 330 housing units at an average density of 3.9/km&amp;sup2; (10.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.41% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.14% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.58% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.14% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.14% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.58% from two or more races.  0.43% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 290 households out of which 23.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 57.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 5.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.4% are non-families. 26.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.37 and the average family size is 2.87.

In the township the population is spread out with 22.0% under the age of 18, 6.2% from 18 to 24, 25.8% from 25 to 44, 30.4% from 45 to 64, and 15.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 106.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 104.2 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $36,111, and the median income for a family is $44,444. Males have a median income of $40,855 versus $21,786 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $17,983.  8.6% of the population and 6.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 5.9% of those under the age of 18 and 5.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
[[Category:St. Louis County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Townships in Minnesota]]

== Name Origins ==

The origin of the name comes from the Embarrass river, where the river was said to embarrass canoeists while they were travelling down the river.</text>
    </revision>
