According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 185.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (71.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  159.3 km&amp;sup2; (61.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 26.2 km&amp;sup2; (10.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 14.10% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,468 people, 582 households, and 439 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 9.2/km&amp;sup2; (23.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 689 housing units at an average density of 4.3/km&amp;sup2; (11.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.09% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.27% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.82% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.27% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.07% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.20% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.27% from two or more races.  0.48% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 582 households out of which 30.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 67.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 3.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.4% are non-families. 19.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.52 and the average family size is 2.90.

In the township the population is spread out with 24.2% under the age of 18, 5.7% from 18 to 24, 28.4% from 25 to 44, 31.4% from 45 to 64, and 10.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 108.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 110.4 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $57,292, and the median income for a family is $62,569. Males have a median income of $41,333 versus $26,579 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $26,202.  4.5% of the population and 3.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.6% of those under the age of 18 and 1.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
[[Category:St. Louis County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Townships in Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
