      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Leonidas''' is a city located in [[St. Louis County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 60.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Leonidas.png|right|Location of Leonidas, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.4 km&amp;sup2; (1.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 4.32% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 60 people, 26 households, and 19 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 17.4/km&amp;sup2; (45.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 27 housing units at an average density of 7.8/km&amp;sup2; (20.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 98.33% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.67% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 26 households out of which 34.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 57.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 3.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 26.9% are non-families. 15.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.31 and the average family size is 2.58.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.3% under the age of 18, 10.0% from 18 to 24, 23.3% from 25 to 44, 30.0% from 45 to 64, and 13.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 100.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 100.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $19,167, and the median income for a family is $19,583. Males have a median income of $31,250 versus $40,000 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,023.  14.3% of the population and 20.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.0% of those under the age of 18 and 14.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
