  <page>
    <title>Proctor, Minnesota</title>
    <id>121786</id>
    <revision>
      <id>32293512</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-21T23:12:10Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>67.1.242.155</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Education */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Proctor''' is a city located in [[St. Louis County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,852.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Proctor.png|right|Location of Proctor, Minnesota]]
[[Image:Downtown_Proctor_MN.jpg|thumb|Downtown Proctor along [[U.S. Highway 2]]]]
Proctor is located beside the Bayview neighborhood of Duluth, with which it forms something of a contiguous community unit due to Bayview's topographical separation (the hill) from adjacent West Duluth.  It is bounded by school rival [[Hermantown, Minnesota|Hermantown]] to the north, [[Midway Township, Minnesota|Midway Township]] to the west, [[Duluth, Minnesota|Duluth]]'s Bayview neighborhood to the east, and a mostly undeveloped area of [[Duluth, Minnesota|Duluth]] (officially in the Riverside neighborhood) to the south.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 7.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  7.8 km&amp;sup2; (3.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 2,852 people, 1,196 households, and 772 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 363.4/km&amp;sup2; (942.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,246 housing units at an average density of 158.8/km&amp;sup2; (411.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.49% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.14% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.16% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.53% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.28% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.40% from two or more races.  0.74% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,196 households out of which 28.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 51.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.4% are non-families. 30.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.38 and the average family size is 2.99.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.0% under the age of 18, 9.4% from 18 to 24, 27.3% from 25 to 44, 23.6% from 45 to 64, and 15.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 86.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 85.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $38,322, and the median income for a family is $49,875. Males have a median income of $33,583 versus $22,035 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,851.  5.0% of the population and 3.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 5.5% of those under the age of 18 and 5.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==

Proctor's school district is [[Independent School District|ISD 704]] (Proctor Public Schools), currently headed by [[superintendent]] Diane Rauschenfels.  The district encompasses not only the city of Proctor, but also the Bayview neighborhood of [[Duluth, Minnesota|Duluth]], and the townships of [[Canosia Township, Minnesota|Canosia]], [[Grand Lake Township, Minnesota|Grand Lake]], [[Midway Township, Minnesota|Midway]], and [[Solway Township, Minnesota|Solway]].  There are three elementary schools (Bayview, Caribou Lake, and Pike Lake), a middle schools, and a high school ([[Proctor High School]]) under the district's control.

==External links==

*[http://www.proctormn.com/ Proctor's Website]

[[Category:St. Louis County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[io:Proctor, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
