      <text xml:space="preserve">'''St. Joseph''' is a city located in [[Stearns County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 4,681.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-St._Joseph.png|right|Location of St. Joseph, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 4.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4.8 km&amp;sup2; (1.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

One of the major landmarks for the city is The College of St. Benedict. A catholic university, the college sticks out in the downtown area due to the high spire of the church itself, and the rotunda and dome of the college. The architecture is different than others, and is clearly visible from miles away.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 4,681 people, 1,120 households, and 712 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 971.7/km&amp;sup2; (2,517.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,147 housing units at an average density of 238.1/km&amp;sup2; (616.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.69% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.21% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.98% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.06% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.38% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.66% from two or more races.  1.22% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,120 households out of which 35.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 36.4% are non-families. 21.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.74 and the average family size is 3.06.

In the city the population is spread out with 16.7% under the age of 18, 44.4% from 18 to 24, 19.8% from 25 to 44, 10.4% from 45 to 64, and 8.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 22 years.  For every 100 females there are 46.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 39.1 males.  Importantly, according to City-Data.com, St. Joseph has the most females in the United States as a percentage of the town's total population.

The median income for a household in the city is $38,938, and the median income for a family is $44,737. Males have a median income of $33,344 versus $22,007 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,011.  20.8% of the population and 5.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 7.7% of those under the age of 18 and 35.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
*[http://stjoseph.govoffice.com/ St. Joseph official website]
*[http://www.city-data.com/city/St.-Joseph-Minnesota.html City-Data.com St. Joseph demographics]

[[Category:Stearns County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[io:St. Joseph, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
