      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Appleton''' is a city located in [[Swift County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,871.  The town is home to a state prison.  It is also home to many retirees and military veterans.  It is notable because it has named all of its twenty-some streets after all dead [[WWII]] veterans of its town.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Appleton.png|right|Location of Appleton, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 5.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  5.2 km&amp;sup2; (2.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 3.40% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 2,871 people, 729 households, and 376 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 557.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,442.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 860 housing units at an average density of 166.9/km&amp;sup2; (432.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 68.13% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 10.73% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.57% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 5.02% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 6.27% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.40% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 5.89% from two or more races.  4.84% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 729 households out of which 23.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 40.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 48.4% are non-families. 45.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 27.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.02 and the average family size is 2.82.

In the city the population is spread out with 12.1% under the age of 18, 9.2% from 18 to 24, 42.7% from 25 to 44, 19.9% from 45 to 64, and 16.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 240.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 266.9 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $25,950, and the median income for a family is $40,313. Males have a median income of $26,991 versus $20,991 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,429.  14.7% of the population and 9.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 14.9% of those under the age of 18 and 23.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:Swift County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Appleton, Minnesota]]</text>
