As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 232 people, 92 households, and 72 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 2.9/km&amp;sup2; (7.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 102 housing units at an average density of 1.3/km&amp;sup2; (3.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 90.95% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.43% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 5.17% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.16% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.29% from two or more races.  2.16% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 92 households out of which 27.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 66.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 21.7% are non-families. 16.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.52 and the average family size is 2.81.

In the township the population is spread out with 22.0% under the age of 18, 3.9% from 18 to 24, 19.8% from 25 to 44, 36.2% from 45 to 64, and 18.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 47 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.7 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $48,125, and the median income for a family is $51,071. Males have a median income of $35,714 versus $21,458 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $20,714.  4.1% of the population and 2.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 0.0% of those under the age of 18 and 13.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
