      <contributor>
        <username>JPizzle1122</username>
        <id>651858</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Geography */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Kerkhoven''' is a city located in [[Swift County, Minnesota]], roughly 100 miles west from the [[Twin Cities]] region of [[Minneapolis]]/[[Saint Paul, Minnesota|St. Paul]] along [[U.S. Highway 12]]. It was incorporated as a city in [[1881]], largely due to the railroad recently built there. As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 759.  [[U.S. Highway 12]] crosses through the city.  Kerkhoven is home to Kerkhoven-Murdock-Sunburg High School on the west side of the community.  The current building (which replaced the 1904 McKinley Building complex) was constructed in 1994.  Kerkhoven's population has declined during the past 50 years due to the decline of agriculture based jobs.  The community is home to Lutheran, Baptist, Methodist, and Evangelical Free churches.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Kerkhoven.png|right|Location of Kerkhoven, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 1.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]), all of which is land - none of the town is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 759 people, 313 households, and 210 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 396.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,023.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 338 housing units at an average density of 176.4/km&amp;sup2; (455.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 94.99% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.13% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.40% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 4.22% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.26% from two or more races.  4.74% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 313 households out of which 31.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 56.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.6% are non-families. 30.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.42 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.3% under the age of 18, 7.0% from 18 to 24, 26.9% from 25 to 44, 18.2% from 45 to 64, and 20.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 85.9 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $32,375, and the median income for a family is $40,179. Males have a median income of $27,262 versus $22,656 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,435.  9.3% of the population and 8.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 15.0% of those under the age of 18 and 7.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
