      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Long Prairie''' is a city located in [[Todd County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,040.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Todd County, Minnesota|Todd County]][[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt;]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Long_Prairie.png|right|Location of Long Prairie, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 6.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.1 km&amp;sup2; (2.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.88% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 3,040 people, 1,229 households, and 769 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 495.3/km&amp;sup2; (1,285.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,334 housing units at an average density of 217.3/km&amp;sup2; (564.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 93.06% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.07% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.74% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.10% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 4.28% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.72% from two or more races.  9.38% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,229 households out of which 29.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 37.4% are non-families. 33.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 19.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.36 and the average family size is 3.01.

In the city the population is spread out with 25.4% under the age of 18, 9.2% from 18 to 24, 24.5% from 25 to 44, 19.8% from 45 to 64, and 21.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 85.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $28,237, and the median income for a family is $35,699. Males have a median income of $31,359 versus $20,152 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $14,386.  16.4% of the population and 13.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 23.1% of those under the age of 18 and 13.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
