      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Geography */ map</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Browns Valley''' is a city located in [[Traverse County, Minnesota]], adjacent to the [[South Dakota]] border.  Browns Valley lies along the [[Little Minnesota River]] between the northern end of [[Big Stone Lake]] and the southern end of [[Lake Traverse]], which is separated from the Little Minnesota River by a low and narrow [[continental divide]] that skirts the northern edge of town.  As of the [[2000]] census, Browns Valley had a total population of 690.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Browns_Valley.png|right|Location of Browns Valley, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.0 km&amp;sup2; (0.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 690 people, 285 households, and 171 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 337.2/km&amp;sup2; (878.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 317 housing units at an average density of 154.9/km&amp;sup2; (403.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 82.61% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 15.80% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.43% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.14% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.14% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.87% from two or more races.  1.74% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 285 households out of which 26.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 45.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 40.0% are non-families. 36.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 3.02.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.5% under the age of 18, 7.4% from 18 to 24, 17.8% from 25 to 44, 19.3% from 45 to 64, and 31.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 45 years.  For every 100 females there are 86.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 82.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $26,563, and the median income for a family is $30,208. Males have a median income of $25,500 versus $20,139 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,062.  14.4% of the population and 10.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 16.5% of those under the age of 18 and 11.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:Traverse County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Browns Valley, Minnesota]]</text>
