      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Walls Township''' is a township located in [[Traverse County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 81.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 94.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (36.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  93.5 km&amp;sup2; (36.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.6 km&amp;sup2; (0.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.61% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 81 people, 28 households, and 22 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 0.9/km&amp;sup2; (2.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 32 housing units at an average density of 0.3/km&amp;sup2; (0.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 100.00% White.

There are 28 households out of which 39.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 78.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 3.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 17.9% are non-families. 10.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.89 and the average family size is 3.22.

In the township the population is spread out with 30.9% under the age of 18, 7.4% from 18 to 24, 24.7% from 25 to 44, 19.8% from 45 to 64, and 17.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 40 years.  For every 100 females there are 92.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 107.4 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $50,000, and the median income for a family is $50,000. Males have a median income of $35,833 versus $23,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $16,820.  0.0% of the population and 0.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].

