  <page>
    <title>Wheaton, Minnesota</title>
    <id>121973</id>
    <revision>
      <id>30205473</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-05T08:56:03Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Poseidon^3</username>
        <id>144758</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Onion Feature</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wheaton''' is a city in [[Traverse County, Minnesota]], [[United States]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,619.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Traverse County, Minnesota|Traverse County]][[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt;]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Wheaton.png|right|Location of Wheaton, Minnesota]]
Wheaton lies along the [[Mustinka River]].  According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 4.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4.6 km&amp;sup2; (1.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,619 people, 747 households, and 434 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 351.2/km&amp;sup2; (909.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 907 housing units at an average density of 196.7/km&amp;sup2; (509.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 99.20% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.37% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.31% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.06% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.06% from two or more races.  1.42% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 747 households out of which 23.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 41.8% are non-families. 39.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 25.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.07 and the average family size is 2.76.

In the city the population is spread out with 21.4% under the age of 18, 5.0% from 18 to 24, 20.7% from 25 to 44, 20.3% from 45 to 64, and 32.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 48 years.  For every 100 females there are 86.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 83.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $29,219, and the median income for a family is $41,827. Males have a median income of $30,313 versus $19,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,181.  10.9% of the population and 7.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 11.7% of those under the age of 18 and 12.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.


== Trivia ==
This town was the subject of a parody article by [[The Onion]] on [[30 November]], [[2005]]. The article described what could be taken as typical small-town Midwestern events as vile debauchery and gross moral violations. [http://www.theonion.com/content/node/43016]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[Category:Traverse County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Wheaton, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
