      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Plainview''' is a city located in [[Wabasha County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,190. The author [[Jon Hassler]] was raised in Plainview and some of the places in his writing are based on the town.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Plainview.png|right|Location of Plainview, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 5.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  5.7 km&amp;sup2; (2.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 3,190 people, 1,157 households, and 824 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 559.8/km&amp;sup2; (1,452.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,223 housing units at an average density of 214.6/km&amp;sup2; (556.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.83% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.03% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.06% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.09% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.45% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.53% from two or more races.  5.14% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,157 households out of which 39.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 58.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.7% are non-families. 24.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.65 and the average family size is 3.16.

In the city the population is spread out with 29.3% under the age of 18, 8.6% from 18 to 24, 28.0% from 25 to 44, 17.9% from 45 to 64, and 16.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $39,952, and the median income for a family is $48,971. Males have a median income of $32,179 versus $22,754 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,494.  6.4% of the population and 5.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.5% of those under the age of 18 and 12.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

