As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 515 people, 174 households, and 135 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 5.7/km&amp;sup2; (14.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 196 housing units at an average density of 2.2/km&amp;sup2; (5.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 94.37% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.14% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.75% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.58% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.19% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.97% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

