According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 108.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (42.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  106.1 km&amp;sup2; (41.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 2.6 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.41% water.

The [[Crow Wing River]] is joined by its [[tributaries]] the [[Leaf River|Leaf]] and [[Partridge River (Crow Wing River)|Partridge]] Rivers in the township.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 714 people, 251 households, and 211 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 6.7/km&amp;sup2; (17.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 311 housing units at an average density of 2.9/km&amp;sup2; (7.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.60% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.14% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.28% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.28% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.70% from two or more races.  0.98% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

