      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Janesville''' is a city located in [[Waseca County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,109.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Janesville.png|right|Location of Janesville, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.3 km&amp;sup2; (1.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 2,109 people, 816 households, and 580 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 636.2/km&amp;sup2; (1,653.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 848 housing units at an average density of 255.8/km&amp;sup2; (664.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.72% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.09% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.38% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.19% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.62% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.00% from two or more races.  1.61% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 816 households out of which 35.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 60.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.9% are non-families. 25.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 12.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.54 and the average family size is 3.05.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.1% under the age of 18, 9.3% from 18 to 24, 28.4% from 25 to 44, 19.2% from 45 to 64, and 16.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $41,667, and the median income for a family is $51,111. Males have a median income of $31,675 versus $21,492 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,443.  3.7% of the population and 1.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 1.4% of those under the age of 18 and 7.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
