      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lake Elmo''' is a city located in [[Washington County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 6,863.  

Much of the area within the city limits is still farmland, so that the city has a very rural feel to it.  However, the city density is likely to increase substantially over the next 15 years, due to a new city plan ordered following loss of a lawsuit against the [[Metropolitan Council]], a regional planning authority.

General information about the city is available from the [http://www.lakeelmo.org City of Lake Elmo].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Lake_Elmo.png|right|Location of Lake Elmo, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 63.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (24.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  59.2 km&amp;sup2; (22.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 4.0 km&amp;sup2; (1.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 6.28% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 6,863 people, 2,347 households, and 1,924 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 116.0/km&amp;sup2; (300.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,389 housing units at an average density of 40.4/km&amp;sup2; (104.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 95.82% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.38% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.29% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.75% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.54% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.22% from two or more races.  1.31% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,347 households out of which 41.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 69.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 18.0% are non-families. 13.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.91 and the average family size is 3.19.

In the city the population is spread out with 29.2% under the age of 18, 7.2% from 18 to 24, 29.3% from 25 to 44, 27.3% from 45 to 64, and 7.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 102.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 101.9 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $76,876, and the median income for a family is $84,562. Males have a median income of $56,667 versus $32,564 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $33,007.  7.3% of the population and 4.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 12.6% of those under the age of 18 and 2.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
