      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Willernie''' is a city located in [[Washington County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 549.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Willernie.png|right|Location of Willernie, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 0.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  0.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 549 people, 225 households, and 146 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 1,630.5/km&amp;sup2; (4,285.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 229 housing units at an average density of 680.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,787.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 93.26% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.91% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.73% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.36% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.36% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.73% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 3.64% from two or more races.  1.09% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 225 households out of which 33.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 43.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 15.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.1% are non-families. 27.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.41 and the average family size is 2.95.

In the city the population is spread out with 25.5% under the age of 18, 6.7% from 18 to 24, 35.5% from 25 to 44, 22.2% from 45 to 64, and 10.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 88.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $42,500, and the median income for a family is $50,313. Males have a median income of $40,625 versus $30,714 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $19,541.  3.9% of the population and 1.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 0.0% of those under the age of 18 and 11.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

