      <minor />
      <comment>[[WP:AWB|AWB assisted]] category emptying per [[WP:CFD|CFD]] [[Wikipedia:Categories for deletion/Log/2006 January 14|Jan 14]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Woodbury''' is an upscale city located in [[Washington County, Minnesota]] and is considered a [[suburb]] of the [[Twin Cities]] metropolitan area. It is situated east of [[Saint Paul, Minnesota|Saint Paul]] along [[Interstate 94]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 46,463.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Woodbury.png|right|Location of Woodbury, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 92.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (35.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  90.6 km&amp;sup2; (35.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.6 km&amp;sup2; (0.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.74% water. When founded, the city was mostly timber but was converted to farm land. Recently, the farm land has given way to [[Urban_development|developments]] and shopping malls.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 46,463 people, 16,676 households, and 12,657 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 512.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,327.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 17,541 housing units at an average density of 193.5/km&amp;sup2; (501.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 90.04% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.51% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.24% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 5.01% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.62% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.56% from two or more races.  2.14% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 16,676 households out of which 43.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 66.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.1% are non-families. 18.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.76 and the average family size is 3.20.

In the city the population is spread out with 30.6% under the age of 18, 5.9% from 18 to 24, 36.9% from 25 to 44, 20.5% from 45 to 64, and 6.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $76,109, and the median income for a family is $84,997. Males have a median income of $60,224 versus $37,676 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $32,606.  1.7% of the population and 0.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 1.2% of those under the age of 18 and 1.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Employment ==
The city's largest employers include [[3M]], whose headquarters are located a few miles west in [[Maplewood, Minnesota|Maplewood]], [[Fortis (finance)|Fortis]], EcoWater, the [[Target Corporation]] and [[State Farm Insurance]]. State Farm's status as a large-scale employer in the city is in question after announcement that their multi-department facility will cease operations and relocate to various regional sites with a total closure of all departments in the facility in [[March]] [[2006]].

==External links==
* [http://www.ci.woodbury.mn.us/ The City of Woodbury]

[[Category:Washington County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[io:Woodbury, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
