== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 90 people, 44 households, and 20 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 386.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,001.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 44 housing units at an average density of 188.8/km&amp;sup2; (489.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 100.00% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]].

There are 44 households out of which 20.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 36.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 52.3% are non-families. 45.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 20.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.05 and the average family size is 2.76.

In the city the population is spread out with 22.2% under the age of 18, 6.7% from 18 to 24, 25.6% from 25 to 44, 21.1% from 45 to 64, and 24.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 150.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 133.3 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $29,375, and the median income for a family is $38,750. Males have a median income of $35,000 versus $20,313 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,941.  36.3% of the population and 27.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 70.8% of those under the age of 18 and 9.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
