      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wolverton Township''' is a township located in [[Wilkin County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 130.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 76.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (29.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  76.9 km&amp;sup2; (29.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 130 people, 50 households, and 43 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 1.7/km&amp;sup2; (4.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 51 housing units at an average density of 0.7/km&amp;sup2; (1.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.46% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.54% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.00% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 50 households out of which 30.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 78.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 4.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 14.0% are non-families. 14.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.60 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the township the population is spread out with 23.1% under the age of 18, 6.2% from 18 to 24, 26.2% from 25 to 44, 26.2% from 45 to 64, and 18.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 103.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 104.1 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $42,500, and the median income for a family is $42,500. Males have a median income of $28,750 versus $22,500 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $18,638.  0.0% of the population and 0.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].

[[Category:Wilkin County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Townships in Minnesota]]</text>
