As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 729 people, 278 households, and 207 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 17.4/km&amp;sup2; (45.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 314 housing units at an average density of 7.5/km&amp;sup2; (19.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 98.77% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.41% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.27% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.55% from two or more races.  0.27% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

