      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Whitewater Township''' is a township located in [[Winona County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the township had a total population of 202.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the township has a total area of 91.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (35.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  91.2 km&amp;sup2; (35.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.37% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 202 people, 65 households, and 52 families residing in the township.  The [[population density]] is 2.2/km&amp;sup2; (5.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 70 housing units at an average density of 0.8/km&amp;sup2; (2.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the township is 97.52% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.99% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.49% from two or more races.  1.98% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 65 households out of which 44.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 70.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 3.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 20.0% are non-families. 16.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.11 and the average family size is 3.56.

In the township the population is spread out with 34.2% under the age of 18, 6.9% from 18 to 24, 30.2% from 25 to 44, 21.3% from 45 to 64, and 7.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 112.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 121.7 males.

The median income for a household in the township is $51,875, and the median income for a family is $58,125. Males have a median income of $28,750 versus $19,167 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the township is $19,122.  0.9% of the population and 0.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 0.0% of those under the age of 18 and 10.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
