      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Albertville''' is a city located in [[Wright County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,621.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Albertville.png|right|Location of Albertville, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 12.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  11.3 km&amp;sup2; (4.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.8 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 6.81% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 3,621 people, 1,287 households, and 984 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 319.2/km&amp;sup2; (826.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,318 housing units at an average density of 116.2/km&amp;sup2; (300.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 98.51% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.30% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.22% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.25% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.08% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.64% from two or more races.  0.66% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,287 households out of which 49.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 61.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 23.5% are non-families. 16.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 2.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.81 and the average family size is 3.21.

In the city the population is spread out with 34.1% under the age of 18, 8.5% from 18 to 24, 41.5% from 25 to 44, 10.8% from 45 to 64, and 5.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 29 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 102.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $58,260, and the median income for a family is $63,578. Males have a median income of $41,783 versus $30,244 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $21,424.  6.9% of the population and 6.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 9.9% of those under the age of 18 and 0.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

