  <page>
    <title>Monticello, Minnesota</title>
    <id>122166</id>
    <revision>
      <id>28256566</id>
      <timestamp>2005-11-14T01:42:09Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Catbar</username>
        <id>33032</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Geography */ map</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Monticello''' is a city located in [[Wright County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 7,868.  Monticello is located on the Mississippi River at the northern edge of Wright County.  The community is home to Nuclear Management Company's Monticello Nuclear Generation Plant.  During winter, hundreds of trumpeter swans nest near Mississippi Drive Park in Monticello as the Mississippi River is heated from warm water discharged by the Monticello Nuclear Generation Plant.  Rapid population growth has led to numerous retail outlets constructed or being planned during 2004-2005, which includes Wal-Mart Supercenter, Target, Muller Family Movie Theatre, Home Depot, Applebee's, Wendy's, and Arby's.  Monticello's local newspaper is the Monticello Times, which can be accessed at [www.monticellotimes.com].


== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Monticello.png|right|Location of Monticello, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 16.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  16.1 km&amp;sup2; (6.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 7,868 people, 2,944 households, and 2,066 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 488.4/km&amp;sup2; (1,264.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,030 housing units at an average density of 188.1/km&amp;sup2; (487.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.96% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.33% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.20% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.55% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.64% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.31% from two or more races.  2.03% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,944 households out of which 43.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 52.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.8% are non-families. 23.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.64 and the average family size is 3.13.

In the city the population is spread out with 31.4% under the age of 18, 9.1% from 18 to 24, 35.4% from 25 to 44, 15.1% from 45 to 64, and 8.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 30 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $45,384, and the median income for a family is $53,566. Males have a median income of $41,057 versus $25,854 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $19,229.  4.6% of the population and 4.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.8% of those under the age of 18 and 7.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]
[[Category:Wright County, Minnesota]]

[[io:Monticello, Minnesota]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
