      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Otsego''' is a city located in [[Wright County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 6,389.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Otsego.png|right|Location of Otsego, Minnesota]]
Otsego is located at the confluence of the [[Mississippi River]] and [[Crow River (Minnesota)|Crow]] Rivers.  According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 78.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (30.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  76.1 km&amp;sup2; (29.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 2.5 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 3.20% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 6,389 people, 2,062 households, and 1,674 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 84.0/km&amp;sup2; (217.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,120 housing units at an average density of 27.9/km&amp;sup2; (72.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.26% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.25% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.36% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.72% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.56% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.85% from two or more races.  1.27% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,062 households out of which 46.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 71.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 5.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 18.8% are non-families. 12.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 2.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.10 and the average family size is 3.41.

In the city the population is spread out with 32.5% under the age of 18, 7.7% from 18 to 24, 34.2% from 25 to 44, 21.4% from 45 to 64, and 4.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 108.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 109.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $57,422, and the median income for a family is $59,319. Males have a median income of $39,568 versus $28,273 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $20,209.  3.2% of the population and 3.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.4% of those under the age of 18 and 13.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

[[Category:Wright County, Minnesota]]
