      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Waverly''' is a city located in [[Wright County, Minnesota]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 732.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MNMap-doton-Waverly.png|right|Location of Waverly, Minnesota]]
According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 4.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.9 km&amp;sup2; (0.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 46.50% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 732 people, 284 households, and 197 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 340.5/km&amp;sup2; (879.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 332 housing units at an average density of 154.4/km&amp;sup2; (399.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 99.18% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.14% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.27% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.41% from two or more races.  0.27% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 284 households out of which 34.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 55.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.3% are non-families. 25.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.58 and the average family size is 3.06.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.2% under the age of 18, 5.2% from 18 to 24, 35.1% from 25 to 44, 19.9% from 45 to 64, and 12.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 96.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 98.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $52,000, and the median income for a family is $57,750. Males have a median income of $39,917 versus $25,815 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $22,552.  4.2% of the population and 1.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.5% of those under the age of 18 and 8.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

Waverly is notable for once having been the home of the former [[Vice President of the United States]], [[Hubert H. Humphrey]].

==External link==
* [http://www.ci.waverly.mn.us/ City of Waverly]

[[Category:Wright County, Minnesota]]
[[Category:Cities in Minnesota]]

[[io:Waverly, Minnesota]]</text>
