      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Farmington''' is a town located in [[Alcorn County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,810. Its [[zip code]] is 38834.

== History ==

Before [[1850]], Farmington was a prosperous village.  Its prosperity suffered a blow, however, when it was bypassed during the construction of the Mobile and Ohio Railroad.

== Geography ==
Farmington is located at 34&amp;deg;55'29&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;26'9&quot; West (34.924792, -88.435931){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 9.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9.7 km&amp;sup2; (3.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.53% water.

===Communities near Farmington===
* [[Burnsville, Mississippi]] - 9.94 [[statute mile]]s
* [[Corinth, Mississippi]] - 3.97 statute miles
* [[Guys, Tennessee]] - 9.41 statute miles
* [[Michie, Tennessee]] - 8.76 statute miles
* [[Ramer, Tennessee]] - 13.61 statute miles

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,810 people, 685 households, and 537 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 186.9/km&amp;sup2; (484.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 746 housing units at an average density of 77.0/km&amp;sup2; (199.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 97.85% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.10% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.06% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.55% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.17% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.28% from two or more races.  0.33% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 685 households out of which 41.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 63.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 21.6% are non-families. 19.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 4.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.64 and the average family size is 3.03.

In the town the population is spread out with 28.3% under the age of 18, 9.0% from 18 to 24, 30.3% from 25 to 44, 23.8% from 45 to 64, and 8.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 100.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.7 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $37,074, and the median income for a family is $41,696. Males have a median income of $29,531 versus $21,346 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $16,327.  4.9% of the population and 4.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.3% of those under the age of 18 and 9.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==See also==
