      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Glen''' is a town located in [[Alcorn County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 286.  Its [[zip code]] is 38846.

== History ==

The town of Glen, located nine miles southeast of [[Corinth, Mississippi|Corinth]], owes its beginning to the Memphis &amp; Charleston Railroad.  Glen was originally called &quot;Glendale,&quot; and is marked as such on old railroad maps.

== Geography ==
Glen is located at 34&amp;deg;51'36&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;25'7&quot; West (34.859967, -88.418633){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 12.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  12.1 km&amp;sup2; (4.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.21% is water.

===Communities near Glen===
* [[Minter City, Mississippi]]
* [[Sumner, Mississippi]]
* [[Webb, Mississippi]]

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 286 people, 121 households, and 87 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 23.6/km&amp;sup2; (61.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 133 housing units at an average density of 11.0/km&amp;sup2; (28.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 99.65% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.35% from two or more races.  0.70% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 121 households out of which 28.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 62.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 27.3% are non-families. 26.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.36 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the town the population is spread out with 22.4% under the age of 18, 7.3% from 18 to 24, 27.6% from 25 to 44, 25.2% from 45 to 64, and 17.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 115.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 113.5 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $26,964, and the median income for a family is $27,813. Males have a median income of $27,083 versus $21,667 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $14,541.  10.4% of the population and 7.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 12.5% of those under the age of 18 and 15.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==

===Public schools===
* [http://www.alcorn.k12.ms.us/ACES/index.htm Alcorn Central Elementary School] - grades K-4 with an enrollment of 508 students
* [http://www.alcorn.k12.ms.us/ACHS/index.htm Alcorn Central High School] - grades 9-12 with an enrollment of 499 students
* [http://www.alcorn.k12.ms.us/ACMS/index.html Alcorn Central Middle School] - grades 5-8 with an enrollment of 514 students

== Transportation ==

===Highways===
* [[U.S. Highway 72]]

==Media==

