      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Kossuth''' is a village located in [[Alcorn County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the village had a total population of 170.  Its [[zip code]] is 38834.

== History ==
Kossuth, located about ten miles southwest of [[Corinth, Mississippi|Corinth]], was founded in the 1840's as &quot;New Hope.&quot;  In [[1852]], the town changed its name to Kossuth in honor of [[Louis Kossuth]], a [[Hungary|Hungarian]] revolutionary hero who led the democratic, anti-Hapsburg Hungarian revolution of 1848. Despite initial success, the democratic state was crushed as Russian Czarist troops descended to attack Hungary and restore the monarchy, executing 13 of Hungary's leading generals in the Transylvanian town of Vilagos under a white flag. 

Kossuth visited the U.S. in [[1851]] after being exiled from his country. He [http://www.americanhungarianfederation.org/images/kossuth_small.jpg Kossuth picture] was greeted enthusiastically and would gain acclaim as one of the greatest orators of all time. Learning English and many other langauges while imprisoned in exile, he would later coin the phrase, &quot;All for the people and all by the people. Nothing about the people without the people. That is Democracy, and that is the ruling tendency of the spirit of our age,&quot; spoken before the Ohio State Legislature, February 16, 1852, given over a decade before Lincoln's famed &quot;for the people, by the people&quot; speech given at Gettysburg in 1863. The renowned Ralph Waldo Emerson said in greeting Kossuth on his arrival at Concord, MA, May 11, 1852:

&quot;[we] have been hungry to see the man whose extraordinary eloquence is seconded by the splendor and the solidity of his actions.&quot; 

Kossuth was only the second foreign leader (second to Gen. Lafayette) to address a joint session of Congress. Kossuth even spawned a fashion craze (moustache-less beard with TopHat) in the ever trendy US. The [http://www.americanhungarianfederation.org American Hungarian Federation] dedicated a bust that now sits proudly in the US Capitol - it reads, &quot;Louis Kossuth, Father of Hungarian Democracy&quot;

== Geography ==
Kossuth is located at 34&amp;deg;52'28&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;38'39&quot; West (34.874561, -88.644184){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the village has a total area of 2.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.5 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

===Communities near Kossuth===
* [[Corinth, Mississippi]] - 8.21 [[statute miles]]s
* [[Rienzi, Mississippi]] - 9.97 statute miles

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 170 people, 73 households, and 57 families residing in the village.  The [[population density]] is 68.4/km&amp;sup2; (177.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 77 housing units at an average density of 31.0/km&amp;sup2; (80.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the village is 98.82% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.59% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.59% from two or more races.  3.53% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 73 households out of which 26.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 74.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 1.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 21.9% are non-families. 20.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.33 and the average family size is 2.67.

In the village the population is spread out with 18.2% under the age of 18, 4.7% from 18 to 24, 25.9% from 25 to 44, 34.7% from 45 to 64, and 16.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 46 years.  For every 100 females there are 109.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 98.6 males.

The median income for a household in the village is $38,750, and the median income for a family is $40,714. Males have a median income of $29,875 versus $23,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the village is $21,131.  3.2% of the population and 2.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 0.0% of those under the age of 18 and 9.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

