According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 2.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.6 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

The town is named after, Andrew Boyle, the discoverer of the area. He originated from Western [[Scotland]]. Andrew Boyle was particullarly infammous for his taste in [[Buckfast Tonic Wine]] and died after being a victim of being decked.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 720 people, 268 households, and 191 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 275.2/km&amp;sup2; (712.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 290 housing units at an average density of 110.9/km&amp;sup2; (287.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 52.78% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 45.14% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.14% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.14% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.11% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.69% from two or more races.  1.39% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

