      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Ackerman''' is a town located in [[Choctaw County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,696.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Choctaw County, Mississippi|Choctaw County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Ackerman is located at 33&amp;deg;18'41&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;10'29&quot; West (33.311400, -89.174745){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 5.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  5.8 km&amp;sup2; (2.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.44% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,696 people, 711 households, and 430 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 291.0/km&amp;sup2; (752.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 781 housing units at an average density of 134.0/km&amp;sup2; (346.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 62.97% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 34.85% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.24% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.59% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.94% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.41% from two or more races.  1.47% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 711 households out of which 29.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 38.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 17.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 39.5% are non-families. 37.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.27 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the town the population is spread out with 24.6% under the age of 18, 7.8% from 18 to 24, 25.8% from 25 to 44, 21.6% from 45 to 64, and 20.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 81.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 76.0 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $21,287, and the median income for a family is $30,511. Males have a median income of $30,588 versus $20,739 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $13,486.  24.7% of the population and 17.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 33.2% of those under the age of 18 and 20.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

