      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Quitman''' is a city located in [[Clarke County, Mississippi]], USA, along the [[Chickasawhay River]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,463.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Clarke County, Mississippi|Clarke County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Quitman is located at 32&amp;deg;2'35&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;43'15&quot; West (32.043004, -88.720867){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 15.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (5.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  13.4 km&amp;sup2; (5.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.9 km&amp;sup2; (0.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 12.37% water.

== Demographics ==
[[Image:Quitman.gif|thumb|left]]
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,463 people, 975 households, and 674 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 183.6/km&amp;sup2; (475.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,097 housing units at an average density of 81.8/km&amp;sup2; (212.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 66.26% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 33.25% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.08% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.04% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.08% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.28% from two or more races.  0.41% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 975 households out of which 29.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 47.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 19.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.8% are non-families. 28.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 12.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.37 and the average family size is 2.87.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.4% under the age of 18, 7.8% from 18 to 24, 22.9% from 25 to 44, 22.5% from 45 to 64, and 22.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 80.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 75.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $30,469, and the median income for a family is $38,311. Males have a median income of $28,250 versus $21,833 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $14,789.  23.3% of the population and 16.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 41.2% of those under the age of 18 and 9.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

