      <text xml:space="preserve">'''West Point''' is a city located in [[Clay County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 12,145.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Clay County, Mississippi|Clay County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
West Point is located at 33&amp;deg;36'22&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;39'9&quot; West (33.606155, -88.652369){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 54.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (21.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  53.9 km&amp;sup2; (20.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.7 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.28% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 12,145 people, 4,567 households, and 3,219 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 225.3/km&amp;sup2; (583.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 4,897 housing units at an average density of 90.9/km&amp;sup2; (235.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 39.91% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 64% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.07% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.22% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.19% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.43% from two or more races.  0.99% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,567 households out of which 35.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 40.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 25.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.5% are non-families. 27.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.57 and the average family size is 3.14.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.9% under the age of 18, 10.7% from 18 to 24, 25.9% from 25 to 44, 20.3% from 45 to 64, and 14.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 82.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 77.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $26,404, and the median income for a family is $32,943. Males have a median income of $30,902 versus $20,255 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,063.  25.1% of the population and 21.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 37.9% of those under the age of 18 and 21.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

West Point is now the home of the 2005-2006 4A football State Champions.  
