      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Clarksdale''' is a city located in [[Coahoma County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 20,645.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Coahoma County, Mississippi|Coahoma County]]{{GR|6}}.

Clarksdale is the official birthplace of the [[blues]] and is home to the internationally known [[Delta Blues Museum]] and &quot;the crossroads&quot;, where some believe [[Robert Johnson]] sold his [[soul]] to the [[devil]] at the stroke of midnight in exchange for the ability to play the blues.  Clarksdale is also the home of actor [[Morgan Freeman]] and boasts his five star restaurant Madidi's and his blues club Ground Zero. It was named in honor of founder and resident [[John Clark]], brother-in-law of politician [[James Lusk Alcorn]], whose plantation home is nearby.

== Geography ==
Clarksdale is located at 34&amp;deg;11'52&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;34'19&quot; West (34.197888, -90.571941){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 35.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (13.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  35.8 km&amp;sup2; (13.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.07% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 20,645 people, 7,233 households, and 5,070 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 575.9/km&amp;sup2; (1,491.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 7,757 housing units at an average density of 216.4/km&amp;sup2; (560.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 29.95% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 68.52% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.11% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.58% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.22% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.60% from two or more races.  0.65% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 7,233 households out of which 36.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 35.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 30.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.9% are non-families. 27.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 12.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.77 and the average family size is 3.38.

In the city the population is spread out with 32.9% under the age of 18, 9.6% from 18 to 24, 25.2% from 25 to 44, 19.3% from 45 to 64, and 12.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 31 years.  For every 100 females there are 81.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 73.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $22,188, and the median income for a family is $26,592. Males have a median income of $26,881 versus $19,918 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,611.  36.2% of the population and 29.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 46.1% of those under the age of 18 and 31.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Famous Clarksdalians==
*[[Sam Cooke]]
*[[John Lee Hooker]]
*[[Ike Turner]]
*[[Nate Dogg]]

