      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Bude''' is a town located in [[Franklin County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,037.

== Geography ==
Bude is located at 31&amp;deg;27'48&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;50'48&quot; West (31.463235, -90.846795){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 3.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.7 km&amp;sup2; (1.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,037 people, 426 households, and 270 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 284.0/km&amp;sup2; (733.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 505 housing units at an average density of 138.3/km&amp;sup2; (357.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 44.17% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 55.06% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.48% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.29% from two or more races.  0.48% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 426 households out of which 35.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 34.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 24.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 36.4% are non-families. 34.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.43 and the average family size is 3.15.

In the town the population is spread out with 30.4% under the age of 18, 9.9% from 18 to 24, 26.6% from 25 to 44, 19.4% from 45 to 64, and 13.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 83.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 77.4 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $16,125, and the median income for a family is $25,000. Males have a median income of $24,063 versus $15,921 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $10,058.  32.2% of the population and 30.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 41.5% of those under the age of 18 and 26.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

