As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 569 people, 199 households, and 153 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 192.7/km&amp;sup2; (498.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 245 housing units at an average density of 83.0/km&amp;sup2; (214.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 39.72% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 58.88% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.35% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.05% from two or more races.  0.53% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

