As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,026 people, 390 households, and 262 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 250.7/km&amp;sup2; (647.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 463 housing units at an average density of 113.1/km&amp;sup2; (292.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 79.92% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 19.40% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.10% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.10% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.49% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.00% from two or more races.  1.07% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 390 households out of which 27.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 51.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.6% are non-families. 29.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.34 and the average family size is 2.92.

In the town the population is spread out with 21.5% under the age of 18, 8.1% from 18 to 24, 19.6% from 25 to 44, 23.5% from 45 to 64, and 27.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 46 years.  For every 100 females there are 71.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 66.0 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $26,731, and the median income for a family is $33,618. Males have a median income of $30,208 versus $19,167 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $14,674.  21.5% of the population and 17.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 38.0% of those under the age of 18 and 12.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

