      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Diamondhead''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Hancock County, Mississippi|Hancock County]], [[Mississippi]], [[USA]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 5,912.

== Geography ==
Diamondhead is located at 30&amp;deg;23'0&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;22'22&quot; West (30.383444, -89.372660){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 30.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (11.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  29.4 km&amp;sup2; (11.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.0 km&amp;sup2; (0.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 3.16% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 5,912 people, 2,559 households, and 1,916 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 201.3/km&amp;sup2; (521.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,084 housing units at an average density of 105.0/km&amp;sup2; (272.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 95.35% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.78% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.41% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.88% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.47% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.08% from two or more races.  2.94% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,559 households out of which 23.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 67.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 5.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.1% are non-families. 21.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.64.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 18.8% under the age of 18, 3.2% from 18 to 24, 23.4% from 25 to 44, 29.8% from 45 to 64, and 24.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 48 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.9 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $51,361, and the median income for a family is $58,533. Males have a median income of $41,725 versus $29,595 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $26,631.  7.2% of the population and 4.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.7% of those under the age of 18 and 2.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

Diamondhead, Hawaii is an extinct volcano located on the island of Oahu in Hawaii.  It has stone steps that many take to the top.  From the top, there is a beautiful view of Wakiki Beach.  Diamondhead, MS was named after this volcano.

