      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Waveland''' is a city located in [[Hancock County, Mississippi]], on the [[Gulf of Mexico]]. As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 6,674. Waveland was the birthplace of [[jazz]] clarinetist [[Johnny Dodds]].

The current mayor of Waveland is [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democrat]] Tommy Longo. 

It is among the areas affected by [[Hurricane Katrina]]. In a news report, state officials said it took a harder hit from the wind and water than any other town along the coast, and that the town was obliterated. [http://www.cnn.com/2005/WEATHER/09/01/obliterated.town.ap/index.html] Waveland was also severely damaged by Hurricane Camille in 1969. The eye of Camille passed directly over Waveland. [http://sciencepolicy.colorado.edu/about_us/meet_us/roger_pielke/camille/report.html]

== Geography ==
Waveland is located at 30&amp;deg;17'23&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;23'1&quot; West (30.289646, -89.383492){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city had a total area of 17.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  17.6 km&amp;sup2; (6.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it was land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there were 6,674 people, 2,731 households, and 1,783 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] was 378.4/km&amp;sup2; (980.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There were 3,442 housing units at an average density of 195.1/km&amp;sup2; (505.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city was 85.38% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 11.21% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.49% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.50% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.49% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.90% from two or more races.  2.02% of the population were [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There were 2,731 households out of which 31.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 46.6% were [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.8% had a female householder with no husband present, and 34.7% were non-families. 29.1% of all households were made up of individuals and 11.7% had someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size was 2.43 and the average family size was 3.01.

In the city the population was spread out with 26.0% under the age of 18, 7.5% from 18 to 24, 28.3% from 25 to 44, 23.9% from 45 to 64, and 14.2% who were 65 years of age or older.  The median age was 38 years.  For every 100 females there were 89.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there were 84.3 males.

The median income for a household in the city was $33,304, and the median income for a family was $38,438. Males had a median income of $29,762 versus $21,694 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city was $16,413.  13.7% of the population and 11.6% of families were below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 15.6% of those under the age of 18 and 11.7% of those 65 and older were living below the poverty line.

The death toll from [[Hurricane Katrina]] for Waveland is not yet known, as they had been hit dead center by the eyewall with a twenty foot storm surge.
The devastation was enormous.

== External links ==
