      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Byram''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Hinds County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 7,386.

== Geography ==
Byram is located at 32&amp;deg;11'39&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;16'12&quot; West (32.194093, -90.270087){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 47.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (18.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  46.2 km&amp;sup2; (17.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.8 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.65% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,386 people, 2,719 households, and 2,180 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 159.9/km&amp;sup2; (414.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,817 housing units at an average density of 61.0/km&amp;sup2; (158.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 85.68% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 13.02% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.19% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.47% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.26% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.37% from two or more races.  0.76% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,719 households out of which 41.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 66.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 19.8% are non-families. 16.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 4.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.72 and the average family size is 3.06.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 27.0% under the age of 18, 7.6% from 18 to 24, 35.3% from 25 to 44, 21.9% from 45 to 64, and 8.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.8 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $54,402, and the median income for a family is $59,014. Males have a median income of $35,673 versus $27,299 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $20,689.  3.4% of the population and 3.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 3.3% of those under the age of 18 and 13.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Legal Battles ==
Since 1991, the bordering city of [[Jackson, Mississippi]] has been attempting to annex the unincorporated portion of Hinds County that has been known as the Byram community since the [[Great Depression]]. (Byram was first incorporated in 1870, but became disincorporated during the Depression.)  That has led to outrage by citizens' desire for low property taxes and what is seen as poor city services (such as slow police response, lack of street repair) by the city of Jackson. In effect, the issue has forced Byram to attempt incorporation to protect itself from annexation by Jackson. All legal funds of the attempt are privately funded. In 2004-05, both sides were in court arguing for their initiatives. After being elected as mayor of Jackson in 2005, [[Frank Melton]] has expressed that he does not wish to actively pursue the matter any further. Despite this, no court dates on the matter were immediately cancelled.

== External links ==
*[http://www.byramonline.com Byram Online]
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|32.194093|-90.270087}}

