      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Isola''' is a town in [[Humphreys County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 768.

== Geography ==
Isola is located at 33&amp;deg;15'45&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;35'37&quot; West (33.262467, -90.593708){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 1.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.9 km&amp;sup2; (0.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 768 people, 279 households, and 191 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 400.7/km&amp;sup2; (1,040.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 307 housing units at an average density of 160.2/km&amp;sup2; (415.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 32.68% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 63.67% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.52% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.73% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.39% from two or more races.  3.12% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 279 households out of which 33.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 38.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 25.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 31.5% are non-families. 28.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.75 and the average family size is 3.37.

In the town the population is spread out with 31.6% under the age of 18, 10.3% from 18 to 24, 24.9% from 25 to 44, 19.0% from 45 to 64, and 14.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 79.2 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $25,063, and the median income for a family is $27,396. Males have a median income of $20,909 versus $17,639 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $13,487.  30.8% of the population and 25.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 48.0% of those under the age of 18 and 18.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

