      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Big Point''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Jackson County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 115.

== Geography ==
Big Point is located at 30&amp;deg;35'13&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;28'55&quot; West (30.586925, -88.481968){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 0.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  0.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 115 people, 41 households, and 38 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 403.7/km&amp;sup2; (1,059.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 42 housing units at an average density of 147.4/km&amp;sup2; (386.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 99.13% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.87% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 41 households out of which 41.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 85.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 4.9% are non-families. 4.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 0.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.80 and the average family size is 2.90.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 25.2% under the age of 18, 9.6% from 18 to 24, 30.4% from 25 to 44, 21.7% from 45 to 64, and 13.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 76.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 75.5 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $30,125, and the median income for a family is $30,125. Males have a median income of $22,361 versus $0 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $10,243.  0.0% of the population and 0.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].

