      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Gautier''' is a city located in [[Jackson County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 11,681.

== Geography ==
Gautier is located at 30&amp;deg;22'54&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;38'39&quot; West (30.381536, -88.644169){{GR|1}}, along [[Mississippi Sound]] of the [[Gulf of Mexico]] at the mouth of the [[Pascagoula River|West Pascagoula River]]. 

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 33.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (12.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  31.7 km&amp;sup2; (12.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.7 km&amp;sup2; (0.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 5.19% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 11,681 people, 4,260 households, and 3,233 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 368.5/km&amp;sup2; (954.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 4,597 housing units at an average density of 145.0/km&amp;sup2; (375.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 68.19% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 27.65% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.51% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.28% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.90% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.42% from two or more races.  3.19% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,260 households out of which 38.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 17.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.1% are non-families. 19.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 4.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.73 and the average family size is 3.11.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.4% under the age of 18, 9.8% from 18 to 24, 30.2% from 25 to 44, 23.3% from 45 to 64, and 8.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 97.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 94.9 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $41,244, and the median income for a family is $46,835. Males have a median income of $33,474 versus $21,622 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,525.  17.3% of the population and 15.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 28.4% of those under the age of 18 and 13.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== History ==
On August 29th 2005 Gautier was one of the many cities devestated by hurricane Katrina. Many of the coastal homes were either destroyed or flooded. Some of the homes along the coast were built on somewhat hilly land leaving those higher on the hill with wind damage only. Homes built right on the water were completely destroyed, occasionally leaving an intact slab, and in a couple of cases the slabs were cracked in half. One home in particular was built on pylons 13 ft. above sea level, and still had the floor ripped out from under the home. Most of northern Gautier above the railroad tracks had severe wind damage, but for the most part remains intact. As many residents recall, Gautier did not receive any damage from Hurricane Camille in 1969, so the damage from Katrina demonstrates how much larger this hurricane was than Camille.

