      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Moss Point''' is a city located in [[Jackson County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 15,851.

== Geography ==
Moss Point is located at 30&amp;deg;24'40&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;31'31&quot; West (30.410999, -88.525140){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 69.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (26.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  64.7 km&amp;sup2; (25.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 4.6 km&amp;sup2; (1.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 6.61% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 15,851 people, 5,714 households, and 4,228 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 244.8/km&amp;sup2; (634.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 6,237 housing units at an average density of 96.3/km&amp;sup2; (249.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 28.04% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 70.56% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.15% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.21% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.44% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.57% from two or more races.  1.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,714 households out of which 31.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 44.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 23.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 26.0% are non-families. 22.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.75 and the average family size is 3.21.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.8% under the age of 18, 9.5% from 18 to 24, 25.8% from 25 to 44, 25.3% from 45 to 64, and 12.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 87.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $32,075, and the median income for a family is $37,712. Males have a median income of $31,126 versus $20,550 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,537.  17.8% of the population and 15.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 23.2% of those under the age of 18 and 17.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Famous People==
Double T the Legally Blind Referee, winner of the 2005 [[RSPW]] Rumble, and senior member of the Milhouse World Order (mWo).

