      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Louin''' is a town located in [[Jasper County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 339.

== Geography ==
Louin is located at 32&amp;deg;4'20&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;15'28&quot; West (32.072112, -89.257890){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 15.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  15.7 km&amp;sup2; (6.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.33% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 339 people, 137 households, and 93 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 21.6/km&amp;sup2; (55.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 164 housing units at an average density of 10.4/km&amp;sup2; (27.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 68.73% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 29.79% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.47% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 137 households out of which 29.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.1% are non-families. 30.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 19.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.47 and the average family size is 3.05.

In the town the population is spread out with 25.4% under the age of 18, 9.4% from 18 to 24, 23.0% from 25 to 44, 20.4% from 45 to 64, and 21.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.1 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $29,583, and the median income for a family is $40,750. Males have a median income of $31,500 versus $21,477 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $17,586.  24.4% of the population and 16.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 53.8% of those under the age of 18 and 9.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

