      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Fayette''' is a city located in [[Jefferson County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,242.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Jefferson County, Mississippi|Jefferson County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Fayette is located at 31&amp;deg;42'40&quot; North, 91&amp;deg;3'44&quot; West (31.711144, -91.062246){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.1 km&amp;sup2; (1.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,242 people, 775 households, and 543 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 733.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,903.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 843 housing units at an average density of 275.8/km&amp;sup2; (715.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 1.92% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 97.37% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.09% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.22% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.40% from two or more races.  0.62% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 775 households out of which 39.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 24.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 40.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.9% are non-families. 27.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 9.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.82 and the average family size is 3.46.

In the city the population is spread out with 34.2% under the age of 18, 12.6% from 18 to 24, 25.6% from 25 to 44, 17.2% from 45 to 64, and 10.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 28 years.  For every 100 females there are 75.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 69.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $13,564, and the median income for a family is $16,875. Males have a median income of $20,500 versus $17,011 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $8,101.  48.2% of the population and 44.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 58.8% of those under the age of 18 and 38.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

