      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Prentiss''' is a town located in [[Jefferson Davis County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,158.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Jefferson Davis County, Mississippi|Jefferson Davis County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Prentiss is located at 31&amp;deg;35'49&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;52'11&quot; West (31.596990, -89.869776){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 4.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4.8 km&amp;sup2; (1.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,158 people, 479 households, and 323 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 239.1/km&amp;sup2; (617.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 537 housing units at an average density of 110.9/km&amp;sup2; (286.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 79.53% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 19.17% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.60% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.09% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.60% from two or more races.  1.47% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 479 households out of which 24.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 50.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.4% are non-families. 30.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 18.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.26 and the average family size is 2.80.

In the town the population is spread out with 19.9% under the age of 18, 7.0% from 18 to 24, 23.9% from 25 to 44, 25.7% from 45 to 64, and 23.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 44 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.3 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $29,200, and the median income for a family is $38,571. Males have a median income of $31,875 versus $21,806 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $18,486.  22.5% of the population and 17.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 47.6% of those under the age of 18 and 9.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

