      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Meridian Station''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Lauderdale County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 1,849.

== Geography ==
Meridian Station is located at 32&amp;deg;32'49&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;37'19&quot; West (32.547017, -88.621981){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 7.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  7.3 km&amp;sup2; (2.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.75% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,849 people, 354 households, and 344 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 253.2/km&amp;sup2; (656.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 526 housing units at an average density of 72.0/km&amp;sup2; (186.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 62.57% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 26.55% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.76% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 2.65% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.32% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.79% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 3.35% from two or more races.  8.06% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 354 households out of which 75.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 88.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 2.8% are non-families. 2.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 0.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.45 and the average family size is 3.49.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 29.1% under the age of 18, 30.4% from 18 to 24, 38.6% from 25 to 44, 1.7% from 45 to 64, and 0.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 22 years.  For every 100 females there are 137.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 145.0 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $42,024, and the median income for a family is $42,173. Males have a median income of $24,348 versus $17,284 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $12,353.  5.9% of the population and 5.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 6.0% of those under the age of 18 and 0.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

