      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Carthage''' is a city located in [[Leake County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 4,637.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Leake County, Mississippi|Leake County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Carthage is located at 32&amp;deg;44'29&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;32'6&quot; West (32.741504, -89.535134){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 24.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (9.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  24.2 km&amp;sup2; (9.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.53% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,637 people, 1,490 households, and 1,065 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 191.5/km&amp;sup2; (495.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,654 housing units at an average density of 68.3/km&amp;sup2; (176.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 52.86% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 44.25% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.04% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.43% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.58% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.82% from two or more races.  1.94% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,490 households out of which 37.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 43.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 23.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.5% are non-families. 25.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.62 and the average family size is 3.12.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.1% under the age of 18, 11.7% from 18 to 24, 28.4% from 25 to 44, 18.1% from 45 to 64, and 15.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 98.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.4 males.

