      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Shannon''' is a town located in [[Lee County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,657.

== Geography ==
Shannon is located at 34&amp;deg;7'1&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;42'5&quot; West (34.116826, -88.701520){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 10.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  10.6 km&amp;sup2; (4.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,657 people, 632 households, and 437 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 155.7/km&amp;sup2; (403.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 691 housing units at an average density of 64.9/km&amp;sup2; (168.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 44.42% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 54.19% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.06% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.12% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.84% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.36% from two or more races.  1.57% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 632 households out of which 40.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 38.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 23.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.7% are non-families. 27.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.62 and the average family size is 3.18.

In the town the population is spread out with 32.0% under the age of 18, 10.6% from 18 to 24, 29.5% from 25 to 44, 19.1% from 45 to 64, and 8.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 29 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.3 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $29,773, and the median income for a family is $30,848. Males have a median income of $25,313 versus $20,149 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $13,592.  18.4% of the population and 16.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 21.6% of those under the age of 18 and 21.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|34.116826|-88.70152}}

[[Category:Lee County, Mississippi]]
[[Category:Towns in Mississippi]]</text>
