      <text xml:space="preserve">'''New Hope''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Lowndes County, Mississippi]], in the [[United States]].  As of the [[United States Census, 2000|2000 census]], the CDP had a total population of 1,964.

== Geography ==
New Hope is located at 33&amp;deg;26'48&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;19'30&quot; West (33.446624, -88.324967){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 6.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.2 km&amp;sup2; (2.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.41% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,964 people, 669 households, and 576 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 314.6/km&amp;sup2; (814.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 695 housing units at an average density of 111.3/km&amp;sup2; (288.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 93.28% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 5.96% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.10% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.10% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.56% from two or more races.  0.15% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 669 households out of which 49.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 73.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 13.9% are non-families. 11.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.93 and the average family size is 3.18.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 31.3% under the age of 18, 6.7% from 18 to 24, 31.9% from 25 to 44, 23.0% from 45 to 64, and 7.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 96.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.9 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $54,375, and the median income for a family is $60,909. Males have a median income of $40,089 versus $26,875 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $25,153.  5.5% of the population and 4.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.8% of those under the age of 18 and 13.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

