      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Holly Springs''' is a city located in [[Marshall County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 7,957.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Marshall County, Mississippi|Marshall County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Holly Springs is located at 34&amp;deg;46'24&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;26'47&quot; West (34.773435, -89.446519){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 33.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (12.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  32.9 km&amp;sup2; (12.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.16% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,957 people, 2,407 households, and 1,699 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 241.9/km&amp;sup2; (626.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,582 housing units at an average density of 78.5/km&amp;sup2; (203.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 22.81% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 76.18% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.06% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.16% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.06% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.69% from two or more races.  0.59% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,407 households out of which 36.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 34.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 31.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.4% are non-families. 27.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.66 and the average family size is 3.22.

In the city the population is spread out with 25.1% under the age of 18, 19.1% from 18 to 24, 27.6% from 25 to 44, 17.2% from 45 to 64, and 11.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 29 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 101.6 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $23,408, and the median income for a family is $25,808. Males have a median income of $29,159 versus $20,777 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,924.  32.0% of the population and 27.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 44.6% of those under the age of 18 and 21.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Health care ==
* [http://www.alliancehealth.us/ Alliance Healthcare System]

==Famous residents==
*[[R. L. Burnside]] (blues musician, 1926-2005)
*[[Ulysses S. Grant]] (1822-1885; wintered in Holly Springs prior to his attack on [[Vicksburg, Mississippi]] during the [[American_Civil_War|Civil War]])
*[[Junior Kimbrough]] (blues musician, 1930-1998)
*[[Ida B. Wells]] (civil rights and anti-lynching activist, 1862-1931; born in Holly Springs)

==Trivia==
* In recent years Holly Springs has been used as a filming location, most notably for [[Robert Altman]]'s ''Cookie's Fortune''.
* Mississippi's highest temperature ever recorded occurred here on July 29, 1930 reaching 115 degrees Fahrenheit.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|34.773435|-89.446519}}

