      <id>27458912</id>
      <timestamp>2005-11-05T17:45:36Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Mithridates</username>
        <id>293296</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>+ido</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Philadelphia''' is a city located in [[Neshoba County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 7,303.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Neshoba County, Mississippi|Neshoba County]]{{GR|6}}.  It is the site of the [[Mississippi Civil Rights Workers Murders]] about which the movie ''[[Mississippi Burning]]'' was written. Philadelphia is also the hometown of Olivia Williams Manning, the mother of current [[NFL]] [[quarterback]]s [[Peyton Manning|Peyton]] and [[Eli Manning]].

In [[1980]] [[Ronald Reagan]] started his presidential election campaign with a speech in Philadelphia at the annual [[county fair]]. On that August day Reagan excited the crowd wild when he announced &quot;I believe in states' rights&quot;. &quot;I believe we have distorted the balance of our government today by giving powers that were never intended to be given in the Constitution to that federal establishment.&quot; He went on to promise to &quot;restore to states and local governments the power that properly belongs to them.&quot; 

== Geography ==
Philadelphia is located at 32&amp;deg;46'27&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;6'46&quot; West (32.774070, -89.112891){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 27.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (10.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  27.5 km&amp;sup2; (10.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.19% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,303 people, 2,950 households, and 1,899 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 265.8/km&amp;sup2; (688.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,302 housing units at an average density of 120.2/km&amp;sup2; (311.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 55.54% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 40.12% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 2.01% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.49% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.08% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.55% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.20% from two or more races.  1.51% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,950 households out of which 30.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 40.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 20.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.6% are non-families. 32.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.38 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.1% under the age of 18, 9.1% from 18 to 24, 25.9% from 25 to 44, 21.0% from 45 to 64, and 17.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 81.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 73.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $26,438, and the median income for a family is $30,756. Males have a median income of $30,731 versus $20,735 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,787.  28.1% of the population and 25.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 41.1% of those under the age of 18 and 16.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

