    <title>Hickory, Mississippi</title>
    <id>122381</id>
    <revision>
      <id>21095047</id>
      <timestamp>2005-08-15T22:12:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>68.62.149.151</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Hickory''' is a town located in [[Newton County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 499. The town is named after [[Andrew Jackson]], nicknamed &quot;Old Hickory,&quot; who passed through the area on his way to fight the [[Battle of New Orleans]] during the [[War of 1812]].

== Geography ==
Hickory is located at 32&amp;deg;19'1&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;1'24&quot; West (32.316880, -89.023376){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 2.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.4 km&amp;sup2; (0.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 499 people, 190 households, and 137 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 207.2/km&amp;sup2; (535.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 207 housing units at an average density of 85.9/km&amp;sup2; (222.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 43.69% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 55.11% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.20% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.00% from two or more races.  0.60% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 190 households out of which 32.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 42.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 24.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 27.4% are non-families. 24.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.63 and the average family size is 3.10.

In the town the population is spread out with 29.3% under the age of 18, 9.6% from 18 to 24, 27.3% from 25 to 44, 18.8% from 45 to 64, and 15.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 80.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 68.1 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $25,417, and the median income for a family is $29,286. Males have a median income of $30,313 versus $20,000 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $11,700.  26.1% of the population and 21.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 32.1% of those under the age of 18 and 39.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
