      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Como''' is a town located in [[Panola County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,310.

== Geography ==
Como is located at 34&amp;deg;30'48&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;56'29&quot; West (34.513343, -89.941290){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 4.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4.9 km&amp;sup2; (1.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.53% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,310 people, 461 households, and 352 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 267.6/km&amp;sup2; (692.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 506 housing units at an average density of 103.4/km&amp;sup2; (267.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 26.79% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 71.83% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.08% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.61% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.69% from two or more races.  1.15% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 461 households out of which 34.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 39.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 31.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 23.6% are non-families. 22.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.84 and the average family size is 3.30.

In the town the population is spread out with 30.1% under the age of 18, 9.8% from 18 to 24, 24.5% from 25 to 44, 20.6% from 45 to 64, and 15.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 81.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 74.8 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $22,344, and the median income for a family is $25,000. Males have a median income of $28,333 versus $18,977 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $12,278.  37.5% of the population and 31.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 57.2% of those under the age of 18 and 29.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

