      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Sardis''' is a town located in [[Panola County, Mississippi]], [[United States]].  As of the [[United States Census, 2000|2000 census]], the town had a total population of 2,038.

== Geography ==
Sardis is located at 34&amp;deg;26'8&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;55'0&quot; West (34.435458, -89.916755){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 5.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  5.1 km&amp;sup2; (2.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,038 people, 790 households, and 493 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 397.4/km&amp;sup2; (1,028.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 862 housing units at an average density of 168.1/km&amp;sup2; (434.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 41.90% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 56.43% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.05% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.39% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.54% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.69% from two or more races.  1.47% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 790 households out of which 25.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 36.1% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 23.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 37.5% are non-families. 33.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 18.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.50 and the average family size is 3.24.

In the town the population is spread out with 26.1% under the age of 18, 9.2% from 18 to 24, 21.2% from 25 to 44, 22.3% from 45 to 64, and 21.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 77.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 72.1 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $23,042, and the median income for a family is $32,933. Males have a median income of $24,783 versus $18,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $15,195.  24.2% of the population and 18.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 32.2% of those under the age of 18 and 24.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

