      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Poplarville''' is a city located in [[Pearl River County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[United States 2000 Census|2000 census]], the city had a total population of 2,601.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Pearl River County, Mississippi|Pearl River County]]{{GR|6}}.

== History ==
[[Theodore G. Bilbo]], US senator noted for his rascist stance was born in Poplarville in [[1877]].

[[Larkin I. Smith]] was born in Poplarville in June [[1944]].

[[Mack Charles Parker]], on trial for rape, was abducted from his Pearl River County jail cell in Popularville in April [[1959]] and lynched, dying of a stab wound to the heart.

On [[September 5]], [[2005]], Popularville played host to a visit by [[George W. Bush]], [[Laura Bush]], and Governor [[Haley Barbour]].  The politicians visited [[Pearl River Community College]] in the aftermath of [[Effect of Hurricane Katrina on Mississippi|Hurricane Katrina]].

== Geography ==
Poplarville is located at 30&amp;deg;50'26&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;32'2&quot; West (30.840507, -89.534021){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 10.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  10.0 km&amp;sup2; (3.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.52% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,601 people, 852 households, and 558 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 260.8/km&amp;sup2; (676.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 936 housing units at an average density of 93.9/km&amp;sup2; (243.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 74.32% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 23.95% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.50% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.15% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.12% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.15% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.81% from two or more races.  0.65% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 852 households out of which 32.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 42.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 19.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 34.4% are non-families. 30.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.37 and the average family size is 2.99.

In the city the population is spread out with 21.6% under the age of 18, 20.8% from 18 to 24, 22.3% from 25 to 44, 18.2% from 45 to 64, and 17.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 84.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 81.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $26,417, and the median income for a family is $32,339. Males have a median income of $35,250 versus $21,667 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,833.  25.3% of the population and 20.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 38.8% of those under the age of 18 and 17.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
