      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Marks''' is a city located in [[Quitman County, Mississippi]], [[United States]].  As of the [[United States Census, 2000|2000 census]], the city had a total population of 1,551.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Quitman County, Mississippi|Quitman County]]{{GR|6}}. Marks is named for Leopold Marx, a Jewish immigrant trader of the late 19th century whose market became one of the earliest centers of business in the area.  

== Geography ==
Marks is located at 34&amp;deg;15'18&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;16'22&quot; West (34.254918, -90.272784){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.7 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,551 people, 579 households, and 387 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 581.4/km&amp;sup2; (1,509.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 643 housing units at an average density of 241.0/km&amp;sup2; (625.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 34.62% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 64.67% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.06% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.19% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.45% from two or more races.  0.39% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 579 households out of which 33.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 32.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 29.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 33.0% are non-families. 29.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.55 and the average family size is 3.16.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.7% under the age of 18, 8.4% from 18 to 24, 26.8% from 25 to 44, 16.7% from 45 to 64, and 19.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 81.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 73.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $20,521, and the median income for a family is $27,153. Males have a median income of $25,100 versus $16,985 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $11,104.  30.3% of the population and 26.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 39.9% of those under the age of 18 and 27.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

