      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Forest''' is a city located in [[Scott County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 5,987.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Scott County, Mississippi|Scott County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Forest is located at 32&amp;deg;21'49&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;28'31&quot; West (32.363627, -89.475348){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 33.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (13.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  33.7 km&amp;sup2; (13.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.15% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 5,987 people, 2,085 households, and 1,478 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 177.7/km&amp;sup2; (460.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,257 housing units at an average density of 67.0/km&amp;sup2; (173.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 40.35% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 50.88% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.40% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.53% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.07% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 5.85% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.92% from two or more races.  12.71% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,085 households out of which 36.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 41.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 24.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.1% are non-families. 23.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.80 and the average family size is 3.25.

In the city the population is spread out with 29.3% under the age of 18, 10.6% from 18 to 24, 27.5% from 25 to 44, 19.7% from 45 to 64, and 13.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $25,638, and the median income for a family is $29,767. Males have a median income of $23,825 versus $17,277 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,484.  23.5% of the population and 21.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 29.5% of those under the age of 18 and 13.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Transportation ==
Forest is served by [[Interstate 20]], [[U.S. Highway 80]], [[Mississippi State Highway 21]], [[Mississippi State Highway 35]], and [[Mississippi State Highway 501]].  Air transportation is available through Forest Municipal or the nearby [[Jackson-Evers International Airport]] (JAN).

== Industry ==
Forest is home to several [[poultry]] processing plants, including Koch Foods, [[Tyson Foods]], and the Forest Packing Company. [[Raytheon]] also has a consolidated manufacturing center in Forest which builds electronic equipment for [[radar]]s and other sensor systems.

== Outdoor recreation ==
* [[Bienville National Forest]]
* [[Roosevelt State Park]]

==Famous residents==
*[[T-Model Ford]] (blues musician, b. 1924)
*[[Todd Pinkston]], [[NFL]] [[wide receiver]], [[Philadelphia Eagles]]

== External links ==
* [http://www.forest-ms.com/ City of Forest, MS website]
* [http://www.fs.fed.us/r8/mississippi/bienville/ Bienville National Forest]
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|32.363627|-89.475348}}

