      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Mize''' is a town located in [[Smith County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 285. The town hosts The Mize Watermelon Festival every July. 
The town used to be known as the capitol of Sullivan's Hollow. It has long had a colorful history known for feuds and lawlessness. 

== Geography ==
Mize is located at 31&amp;deg;52'2&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;33'16&quot; West (31.867332, -89.554331){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 6.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.0 km&amp;sup2; (2.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 285 people, 117 households, and 71 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 47.2/km&amp;sup2; (122.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 132 housing units at an average density of 21.9/km&amp;sup2; (56.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 97.54% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.75% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.35% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.35% from two or more races.  1.05% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 117 households out of which 31.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 50.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 38.5% are non-families. 36.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.44 and the average family size is 3.25.

In the town the population is spread out with 28.4% under the age of 18, 6.7% from 18 to 24, 25.3% from 25 to 44, 22.5% from 45 to 64, and 17.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 82.1 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $20,000, and the median income for a family is $35,625. Males have a median income of $30,714 versus $14,688 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $12,647.  28.3% of the population and 26.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 38.1% of those under the age of 18 and 32.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

