      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Charleston''' is a city in North Central [[Mississippi]] and one of the county seats of [[Tallahatchie County, Mississippi|Tallahatchie County]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,198.

== Geography ==
Charleston is located at 34&amp;deg;0'27&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;3'14&quot; West (34.007514, -90.054009){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.5 km&amp;sup2; (1.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.73% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,198 people, 848 households, and 569 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 624.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,612.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 933 housing units at an average density of 264.9/km&amp;sup2; (684.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 39.26% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 59.69% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.36% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.05% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.64% from two or more races.  1.55% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 848 households out of which 29.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 33.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 28.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.8% are non-families. 31.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.51 and the average family size is 3.14.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.4% under the age of 18, 9.1% from 18 to 24, 25.2% from 25 to 44, 20.1% from 45 to 64, and 18.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 79.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 72.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $18,208, and the median income for a family is $24,750. Males have a median income of $26,500 versus $16,406 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $10,835.  34.4% of the population and 30.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 49.4% of those under the age of 18 and 29.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

