      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Webb''' is a town located in [[Tallahatchie County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 587.

==History==

Webb was founded around [[1880]]. The first post office was founded in 1880 and named '''Hood''' for one of the earlier settlers. In [[1882]], Judge J.L. Webb operated the only store there and later the Hood Masonic Lodge was built. There was one saloon at that time called &quot;The Razzle Dazzle&quot;. The town was incorporated in [[1905]].

In those days most of the groceries and necessities were brought to Hood by flat bottom boat from Sharkey, being hauled down the river from Friars Point. Cassidy Bayou was navigable then and was maintained by the government from Sharkey to Hood. The town was later renamed in honor of Judge Webb.

== Geography ==
Webb is located at 33&amp;deg;56'49&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;20'43&quot; West (33.947045, -90.345304){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 1.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 587 people, 225 households, and 135 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 527.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,380.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 251 housing units at an average density of 225.4/km&amp;sup2; (590.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 35.09% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 61.33% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 2.04% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.53% from two or more races.  0.85% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 225 households out of which 26.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 33.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 20.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 40.0% are non-families. 35.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.61 and the average family size is 3.47.

In the town the population is spread out with 26.1% under the age of 18, 12.9% from 18 to 24, 26.4% from 25 to 44, 18.6% from 45 to 64, and 16.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.4 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $25,000, and the median income for a family is $29,063. Males have a median income of $26,500 versus $23,125 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $12,272.  26.6% of the population and 16.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 39.4% of those under the age of 18 and 26.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

