      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Golden''' is a town located in [[Tishomingo County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 201.  Its [[zip code]] is 38847.

== History ==

The community of Golden originally sprang up around Golden Sawmill.  Almost all of the inhabitants of Golden were employed by the sawmill, and its decline corresponded with a decline in the town's prosperity.  The building of the railroad in the early 1900's brought new life to the town and it was incorporated on [[February 8]], [[1908]].  The town was named for the baby of one of the area's early settlers, Golden Patrie Wiggins.

== Geography ==
Golden is located at 34&amp;deg;29'14&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;11'15&quot; West (34.487217, -88.187427){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 1.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.5 km&amp;sup2; (0.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

=== Communities near Golden ===
* [[Belmont, Mississippi]] - 2.29 [[statute mile]]s
* [[Red Bay, Alabama]] - 3.92 statute miles
* [[Vina, Alabama]] - 10.29 statute miles

