      <text xml:space="preserve">'''North Tunica''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Tunica County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 1,450.

== Geography ==
North Tunica is located at 34&amp;deg;42'6&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;22'42&quot; West (34.701643, -90.378253){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 1.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.9 km&amp;sup2; (0.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,450 people, 425 households, and 333 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 777.6/km&amp;sup2; (2,014.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 449 housing units at an average density of 240.8/km&amp;sup2; (623.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 4.69% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 94.90% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.21% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.21% from two or more races.  0.41% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 425 households out of which 40.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 26.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 46.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 21.6% are non-families. 19.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 9.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.29 and the average family size is 3.76.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 36.4% under the age of 18, 13.6% from 18 to 24, 25.2% from 25 to 44, 15.8% from 45 to 64, and 9.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 25 years.  For every 100 females there are 82.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 75.3 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $14,891, and the median income for a family is $16,466. Males have a median income of $16,250 versus $16,985 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $6,972.  50.7% of the population and 45.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 60.1% of those under the age of 18 and 31.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

