      <comment>/* External links */ new article link</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Tunica''' is a town located in [[Tunica County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,132.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Tunica County, Mississippi|Tunica County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Tunica is located at 34&amp;deg;41'20&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;22'50&quot; West (34.688797, -90.380587){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 1.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.8 km&amp;sup2; (0.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,132 people, 537 households, and 254 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 615.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,588.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 592 housing units at an average density of 321.9/km&amp;sup2; (830.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 67.84% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 29.42% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.27% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.06% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.88% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.53% from two or more races.  2.30% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 537 households out of which 18.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 34.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 52.7% are non-families. 48.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 26.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.01 and the average family size is 2.94.

In the town the population is spread out with 18.9% under the age of 18, 6.1% from 18 to 24, 23.4% from 25 to 44, 28.3% from 45 to 64, and 23.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 46 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 80.0 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $26,607, and the median income for a family is $54,583. Males have a median income of $30,208 versus $22,250 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $20,114.  25.5% of the population and 17.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 33.3% of those under the age of 18 and 21.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Casinos ==
The town's name is popularly associated with multiple [[casino]]s in close proximity to the [[Mississippi River]], though the current group of casinos actually starts in the community of [[Tunica Resorts, Mississippi|Tunica Resorts]], north of the town of Tunica, and extending to the [[DeSoto County, Mississippi|DeSoto County]] line. Tunica Resorts was originally named [[Robinsonville, Mississippi|Robinsonville]], but the name was changed in [[2005]] to eliminate confusion over the location of the casinos, which have always used the name &quot;Tunica&quot; in reference to their location.  Success of these gaming houses came at the expense of the area's first group of casinos in the early 1990s, located just northwest of Tunica proper, in an area known as Mhoon Landing — much of what comprises the current [[census designated place]] of [[North Tunica, Mississippi|North Tunica]]. These casinos were closed or moved as larger resorts opened closer to [[Memphis, Tennessee]].

Unlike the area including casinos along Mississipi's Gulf Coast region, Tunica was not in the path of [[Hurricane Katrina]].  As a result, some of the regular Gulf Coast customer traffic from casinos has drifted northward to Tunica County.

Though the casinos lie outside of the town limits, the effects of tax revenue generated is notably felt inside the town.  Major improvements to the public school system and downtown district are among the most visible aspects currently; long-term effects include major highway improvements on U. S. Highway 61 and a much-discussed potential expansion of the municipal airport.

== External links ==
