== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,109 people, 386 households, and 272 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 428.2/km&amp;sup2; (1,110.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 417 housing units at an average density of 161.0/km&amp;sup2; (417.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 1.17% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 97.57% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.27% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.36% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.63% from two or more races.  0.63% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 386 households out of which 44.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 23.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 43.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.5% are non-families. 27.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 9.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.87 and the average family size is 3.54.

In the town the population is spread out with 40.8% under the age of 18, 11.6% from 18 to 24, 24.0% from 25 to 44, 16.3% from 45 to 64, and 7.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 23 years.  For every 100 females there are 75.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 56.4 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $15,000, and the median income for a family is $18,295. Males have a median income of $21,307 versus $16,793 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $8,050.  47.4% of the population and 43.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 58.9% of those under the age of 18 and 53.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

