      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Eupora''' is a city located in [[Webster County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,326.

== Geography ==
Eupora is located at 33&amp;deg;32'30&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;16'20&quot; West (33.541604, -89.272121){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 9.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  8.4 km&amp;sup2; (3.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.8 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 8.94% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,326 people, 877 households, and 590 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 275.5/km&amp;sup2; (714.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 957 housing units at an average density of 113.3/km&amp;sup2; (293.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 58.86% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 38.01% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.13% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.17% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.28% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.56% from two or more races.  3.74% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 877 households out of which 31.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 41.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 21.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.7% are non-families. 30.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.47 and the average family size is 3.08.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.1% under the age of 18, 9.3% from 18 to 24, 24.5% from 25 to 44, 18.1% from 45 to 64, and 22.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 79.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 74.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $24,839, and the median income for a family is $37,950. Males have a median income of $26,875 versus $21,458 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,927.  24.0% of the population and 20.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 35.6% of those under the age of 18 and 16.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Famous Eupora Natives ==
* [[Thomas Abernathy]], former U.S. Congressmen
* [[Glenda Shaw Brown]], portrait artist
* [[Charlie Carroll]], former Miss Mississippi
* [[Paige Cothran]], writer and former NFL player
* [[John Jameson]], lobbyist
* [[Marckell Patterson]], professional basketball player
* [[Charlie Ross]], state senator and candidate for Lt. Governor

