      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Walthall''' is a village located in [[Webster County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the village had a total population of 170.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Webster County, Mississippi|Webster County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Walthall is located at 33&amp;deg;36'24&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;16'44&quot; West (33.606588, -89.279000){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the village has a total area of 2.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.5 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 170 people, 61 households, and 50 families residing in the village.  The [[population density]] is 67.0/km&amp;sup2; (173.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 69 housing units at an average density of 27.2/km&amp;sup2; (70.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the village is 92.94% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.53% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.59% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.59% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.35% from two or more races.  1.18% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 61 households out of which 41.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 68.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 18.0% are non-families. 18.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 9.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.79 and the average family size is 3.18.

In the village the population is spread out with 31.8% under the age of 18, 10.6% from 18 to 24, 25.3% from 25 to 44, 21.2% from 45 to 64, and 11.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 30 years.  For every 100 females there are 107.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.3 males.

The median income for a household in the village is $31,000, and the median income for a family is $36,875. Males have a median income of $30,417 versus $23,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the village is $14,903.  21.2% of the population and 24.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 22.4% of those under the age of 18 and 57.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

