      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Louisville''' is a city located in [[Winston County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 7,006.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Winston County, Mississippi|Winston County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
Louisville is located at 33&amp;deg;7'23&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;3'22&quot; West (33.122931, -89.056182){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 39.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (15.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  39.1 km&amp;sup2; (15.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.6 km&amp;sup2; (0.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.44% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,006 people, 2,641 households, and 1,817 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 179.4/km&amp;sup2; (464.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,884 housing units at an average density of 73.8/km&amp;sup2; (191.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 46.29% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 52.46% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.13% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.17% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.44% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.51% from two or more races.  1.66% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,641 households out of which 34.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 40.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 25.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 31.2% are non-families. 28.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.55 and the average family size is 3.12.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.9% under the age of 18, 9.3% from 18 to 24, 24.7% from 25 to 44, 19.8% from 45 to 64, and 17.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 80.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 73.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $27,485, and the median income for a family is $31,750. Males have a median income of $29,951 versus $17,491 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,857.  28.5% of the population and 24.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 39.3% of those under the age of 18 and 20.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

