      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Bentonia''' is a town located in [[Yazoo County, Mississippi]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 500.  Some blues scholars maintain that there is a &quot;[[Bentonia School (blues)|Bentonia School]]&quot; of blues singing and guitar-playing, and that &quot;Bentonia-style&quot; is a distinct style of [[Delta Blues]], but Bentonia lies outside the [[Mississippi Delta]] proper.  

== Geography ==
Bentonia is located at {{coor dms|32|38|38|N|90|22|5|W|type:city}} (32.643889, -90.368121){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 3.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.5 km&amp;sup2; (1.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

