As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 280 people, 124 households, and 73 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 308.9/km&amp;sup2; (796.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 142 housing units at an average density of 156.6/km&amp;sup2; (404.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.14% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.36% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.50% from two or more races.  1.43% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 124 households out of which 30.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 47.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 41.1% are non-families. 36.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 23.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.26 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.4% under the age of 18, 5.7% from 18 to 24, 25.4% from 25 to 44, 26.1% from 45 to 64, and 16.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 98.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $21,750, and the median income for a family is $32,500. Males have a median income of $19,479 versus $22,500 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $11,763.  26.5% of the population and 20.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 39.7% of those under the age of 18 and 31.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

