      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lamar''' is a city located in [[Barton County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 4,425.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Barton County, Missouri|Barton County]]{{GR|6}}.

== History ==

Lamar is the birthplace of [[President of the United States|President]] [[Harry S. Truman]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Lamar.png|right|Location of Lamar, Missouri]]

Lamar is located at 37&amp;deg;29'37&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;16'20&quot; West (37.493676, -94.272111){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 10.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9.9 km&amp;sup2; (3.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.8 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 7.25% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,425 people, 1,835 households, and 1,154 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 446.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,154.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,995 housing units at an average density of 201.1/km&amp;sup2; (520.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.61% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.18% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.61% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.34% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.14% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.34% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.79% from two or more races.  1.40% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,835 households out of which 32.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 37.1% are non-families. 33.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 18.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.35 and the average family size is 2.98.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.6% under the age of 18, 8.5% from 18 to 24, 24.9% from 25 to 44, 19.5% from 45 to 64, and 20.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 80.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $29,296, and the median income for a family is $38,007. Males have a median income of $26,375 versus $20,688 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,684.  12.1% of the population and 9.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 11.0% of those under the age of 18 and 17.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

