      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Belton''' is a city in [[Cass County, Missouri]], near [[Kansas City, Missouri|Kansas City]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a population of 21,730.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Belton.png|right|Location of Belton, Missouri]]

Belton is at 38&amp;deg;49'6&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;31'47&quot; West (38.818232, -94.529838){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 34.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (13.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  34.7 km&amp;sup2; (13.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.30% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 21,730 people, 7,945 households, and 5,807 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 626.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,622.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 8,411 housing units at an average density of 242.4/km&amp;sup2; (627.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  

===Racial makeup===
The racial makeup of the city is 92.98% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.86% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.59% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.59% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.08% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.07% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.84% from two or more races.  4.68% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

===Households===
There are 7,945 households, out of which 40.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 56.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 26.9% are non-families. 22.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.70 and the average family size is 3.15.

The population is spread out with 30.0% under the age of 18, 8.6% from 18 to 24, 32.6% from 25 to 44, 18.8% from 45 to 64, and 10.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.1 males.

===Income===

The median income for a household in the city is $45,581, and the median income for a family is $51,268. Males have a median income of $35,518 versus $25,542 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,572.  7.9% of the population and 6.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.5% of those under the age of 18 and 4.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

