      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Freeman''' is a city located in [[Cass County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 521.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Freeman.png|right|Location of Freeman, Missouri]]

Freeman is located at 38&amp;deg;37'4&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;30'25&quot; West (38.617820, -94.507068){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 1.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.5 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 521 people, 172 households, and 142 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 437.3/km&amp;sup2; (1,121.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 186 housing units at an average density of 156.1/km&amp;sup2; (400.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.70% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.19% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.34% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.19% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.58% from two or more races.  0.77% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 172 households out of which 41.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 64.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 15.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 17.4% are non-families. 14.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.01 and the average family size is 3.30.

In the city the population is spread out with 32.4% under the age of 18, 8.1% from 18 to 24, 32.2% from 25 to 44, 15.7% from 45 to 64, and 11.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.3 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $46,339, and the median income for a family is $48,500. Males have a median income of $33,750 versus $23,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,450.  9.1% of the population and 5.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 13.9% of those under the age of 18 and 4.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

