      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Brunswick''' is a city located in [[Chariton County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 925. Brunswick is home to the world's largest [[pecan]] (made of concrete).

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Brunswick.png|right|Location of Brunswick, Missouri]]

Brunswick is located at 39&amp;deg;25'25&quot; North, 93&amp;deg;7'44&quot; West (39.423563, -93.128819){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.1 km&amp;sup2; (1.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 4.03% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 925 people, 426 households, and 242 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 300.1/km&amp;sup2; (776.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 536 housing units at an average density of 173.9/km&amp;sup2; (450.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 86.16% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 13.30% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.32% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.22% from two or more races.  0.86% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 426 households out of which 20.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 44.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 43.0% are non-families. 39.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 26.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.09 and the average family size is 2.74.

