      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Nixa''' is a city located in [[Christian County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 12,124.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Nixa.png|right|Location of Nixa, Missouri]]

Nixa is located at 37&amp;deg;2'43&quot; North, 93&amp;deg;17'56&quot; West (37.045253, -93.298755){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 16.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  16.0 km&amp;sup2; (6.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
[[Image:Nixa.jpg|thumb|left]]
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 12,124 people, 4,654 households, and 3,448 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 759.9/km&amp;sup2; (1,969.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 4,962 housing units at an average density of 311.0/km&amp;sup2; (805.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.43% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.46% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.36% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.43% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.30% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.01% from two or more races.  1.26% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,654 households out of which 40.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 58.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.9% are non-families. 20.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.56 and the average family size is 2.95.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.4% under the age of 18, 8.5% from 18 to 24, 34.5% from 25 to 44, 17.2% from 45 to 64, and 11.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 89.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.9 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $37,655, and the median income for a family is $44,556. Males have a median income of $33,636 versus $21,737 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,774.  9.7% of the population and 8.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 14.3% of those under the age of 18 and 6.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==
All of the schools in Nixa are public. Currently, the Nixa R-2 School District operates four elementary schools for students in kindergarten through fourth grade, two elementary schools for students in the fifth and sixth grades, one junior high school, and one high school. The district is widely considered one of the best in Missouri and has received the Missouri Department of Elementary and Secondary Education's Distinction in Performance award.

== Movies ==
In the 2004 film The Bourne Supremacy it is revealed at the very end of the movie that Jason Bourne's real name is David Webb and that he was born in Nixa, Missouri.

