      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Spokane''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Christian County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 133.  The name is not pronounced like [[Spokane, Washington]]; instead, the &quot;a&quot; is long (that is, &quot;spō-kān&quot;) and rhymes with &quot;cane&quot;.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Spokane.png|right|Location of Spokane, Missouri]]

Spokane is located at 36&amp;deg;51'43&quot; North, 93&amp;deg;18'15&quot; West (36.861839, -93.304152){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 2.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.0 km&amp;sup2; (0.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 133 people, 38 households, and 34 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 65.0/km&amp;sup2; (168.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 46 housing units at an average density of 22.5/km&amp;sup2; (58.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 97.74% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 2.26% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.00% from two or more races.  0.75% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 38 households out of which 63.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 78.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 7.9% are non-families. 7.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.50 and the average family size is 3.69.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 42.1% under the age of 18, 5.3% from 18 to 24, 30.8% from 25 to 44, 16.5% from 45 to 64, and 5.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 28 years.  For every 100 females there are 98.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 97.4 males.

