      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Kearney''' is a city located in [[Clay County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 5,472. It is most famous for being the birthplace of [[Jesse James]].  There is also an annual festival to honor the train robber.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Kearney.png|right|Location of Kearney, Missouri]]

Kearney is located at 39&amp;deg;21'57&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;21'37&quot; West (39.365845, -94.360239){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 17.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  17.0 km&amp;sup2; (6.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.


== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 5,472 people, 1,910 households, and 1,495 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 321.6/km&amp;sup2; (833.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,995 housing units at an average density of 117.2/km&amp;sup2; (303.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 98.3% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.90% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.4% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.2% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian or [pacific islander])0.55% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.15% from two or more races.  1.9% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,910 households out of which 49.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 63.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 21.7% are non-families. 18.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.84 and the average family size is 3.24.

In the city the population is spread out with 33.6% under the age of 18, 6.4% from 18 to 24, 35.4% from 25 to 44, 16.3% from 45 to 64, and 8.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 31 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.7 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $56,603, and the median income for a family is $64,540. Males have a median income of $45,721 versus $26,739 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $21,147.  2.5% of the population and 1.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.3% of those under the age of 18 and 5.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

