      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Boonville''' is a city located in [[Cooper County, Missouri]], USA.  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 8,202.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Cooper County, Missouri|Cooper County]]{{GR|6}}. It is the birthplace of country singer [[Sara Evans]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Boonville.png|right|Location of Boonville, Missouri]]

Boonville is located at 38&amp;deg;57'54&quot; North, 92&amp;deg;44'30&quot; West (38.965017, -92.741757){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 19.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (7.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  17.8 km&amp;sup2; (6.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 6.26% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 8,202 people, 2,667 households, and 1,696 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 459.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,190.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,041 housing units at an average density of 170.4/km&amp;sup2; (441.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 80.22% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 16.84% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.51% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.41% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.40% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.57% from two or more races.  1.23% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,667 households out of which 30.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 36.4% are non-families. 31.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.33 and the average family size is 2.93.

In the city the population is spread out with 19.6% under the age of 18, 20.8% from 18 to 24, 27.4% from 25 to 44, 16.7% from 45 to 64, and 15.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 30 years.  For every 100 females there are 138.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 146.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $33,440, and the median income for a family is $40,294. Males have a median income of $28,498 versus $20,739 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $14,854.  11.3% of the population and 9.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 13.4% of those under the age of 18 and 6.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Recreation ==

Boonville is near the middle of the [[Katy Trail State Park|Katy Trail]], a 225 mile long state park enjoyed by cyclists and hikers.

== External links ==

* [http://www.bikekatytrail.com/ Katy Trail Information]

