There are 93 households out of which 26.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 64.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 4.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.0% are non-families. 23.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 12.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.41 and the average family size is 2.82.

In the village the population is spread out with 21.9% under the age of 18, 10.7% from 18 to 24, 24.6% from 25 to 44, 23.2% from 45 to 64, and 19.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.2 males.

The median income for a household in the village is $27,000, and the median income for a family is $30,000. Males have a median income of $21,250 versus $15,000 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the village is $11,135.  16.0% of the population and 19.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 13.4% of those under the age of 18 and 15.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

