      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Union''' is a city located in [[Franklin County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 7,757.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Franklin County, Missouri|Franklin County]]{{GR|6}}.  It is located on the [[Bourbeuse River]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Union.png|right|Location of Union, Missouri]]

Union is located at 38&amp;deg;26'48&quot; North, 91&amp;deg;0'22&quot; West (38.446684, -91.006070){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 20.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (8.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  20.9 km&amp;sup2; (8.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,757 people, 2,940 households, and 2,002 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 370.7/km&amp;sup2; (959.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,133 housing units at an average density of 149.7/km&amp;sup2; (387.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.44% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.43% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.30% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.17% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.23% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.43% from two or more races.  0.99% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,940 households out of which 35.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 52.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 31.9% are non-families. 26.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.56 and the average family size is 3.10.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.6% under the age of 18, 9.3% from 18 to 24, 31.0% from 25 to 44, 19.1% from 45 to 64, and 13.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $39,596, and the median income for a family is $44,474. Males have a median income of $31,852 versus $22,924 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,885.  7.2% of the population and 4.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.8% of those under the age of 18 and 11.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Government ==
The current mayor of Union is Mayor Glenn Van Leer.  The city is divided into wards.  Aldermen are elected from these wards and sit on the Board of Aldermen.

