      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Ridgeway''' is a city located in [[Harrison County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 530.


== Headline text ==
the ridgeway is the border between scotland and england

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 530 people, 221 households, and 146 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 179.5/km&amp;sup2; (464.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 261 housing units at an average density of 88.4/km&amp;sup2; (228.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.55% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.94% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.57% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.94% from two or more races.  2.08% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 221 households out of which 26.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 52.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 33.5% are non-families. 29.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.40 and the average family size is 2.92.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.0% under the age of 18, 10.6% from 18 to 24, 20.6% from 25 to 44, 24.3% from 45 to 64, and 20.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 95.6 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $19,844, and the median income for a family is $26,250. Males have a median income of $27,500 versus $16,094 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,551.  22.7% of the population and 17.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 28.7% of those under the age of 18 and 11.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

