      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Big Lake''' is a village located in [[Holt County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the village had a total population of 127.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Big_Lake.png|right|Location of Big Lake, Missouri]]

Big Lake is located at 40&amp;deg;4'24&quot; North, 95&amp;deg;21'3&quot; West (40.073443, -95.350863){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the village has a total area of 6.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4.4 km&amp;sup2; (1.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 2.5 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 36.23% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 127 people, 60 households, and 37 families residing in the village.  The [[population density]] is 29.0/km&amp;sup2; (75.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 376 housing units at an average density of 85.9/km&amp;sup2; (222.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the village is 98.43% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.79% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.79% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

