      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Fayette''' is a city located in [[Howard County, Missouri]], USA.  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,793.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Howard County, Missouri|Howard County]]{{GR|6}}.  It is also the home of [[Central Methodist College]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Fayette.png|right|Location of Fayette, Missouri]]

Fayette is located at 39&amp;deg;8'44&quot; North, 92&amp;deg;41'10&quot; West (39.145468, -92.686126){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 5.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  5.8 km&amp;sup2; (2.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

The campus of [[Central Methodist College]] is central to the town.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,793 people, 976 households, and 578 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 483.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,253.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,133 housing units at an average density of 196.2/km&amp;sup2; (508.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 79.16% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 18.33% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.47% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.21% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.47% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.32% from two or more races.  0.93% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 976 households out of which 25.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 41.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 40.7% are non-families. 34.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.18 and the average family size is 2.79.

In the city the population is spread out with 17.9% under the age of 18, 28.2% from 18 to 24, 19.5% from 25 to 44, 16.2% from 45 to 64, and 18.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 29 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.3 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $27,276, and the median income for a family is $35,694. Males have a median income of $27,768 versus $20,833 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $13,451.  15.6% of the population and 9.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 18.1% of those under the age of 18 and 20.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

