      <text xml:space="preserve">'''West Plains''' is a city located in [[Howell County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 10,866.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Howell County, Missouri|Howell County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-West Plains.png|right|Location of West_Plains, Missouri]]

West Plains is located at 36&amp;deg;44'14&quot; North, 91&amp;deg;51'54&quot; West (36.737355, -91.864991){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 32.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (12.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  32.0 km&amp;sup2; (12.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.16% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 10,866 people, 4,518 households, and 2,909 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 339.4/km&amp;sup2; (879.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 5,072 housing units at an average density of 158.4/km&amp;sup2; (410.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 95.72% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.73% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.96% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.71% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.06% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.52% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.31% from two or more races.  1.65% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,518 households out of which 31.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.6% are non-families. 32.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.87.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.8% under the age of 18, 8.7% from 18 to 24, 25.6% from 25 to 44, 19.6% from 45 to 64, and 21.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 83.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 77.0 males.

