      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>/* Demographics */  updated CSHS link</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Carthage''' is a city located in [[Jasper County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 12,668.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Jasper County, Missouri|Jasper County]]{{GR|6}}

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Carthage.png|right|Location of Carthage, Missouri]]

Carthage is located at 37&amp;deg;10'4&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;18'54&quot; West (37.167773, -94.314958){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 24.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (9.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  24.7 km&amp;sup2; (9.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.42% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2002]], there are 13,316 people, 4,813 households, and 3,157 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 512.7/km&amp;sup2; (1,328.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 5,217 housing units at an average density of 211.1/km&amp;sup2; (547.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 86.71% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.54% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.05% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.59% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.21% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 6.65% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.25% from two or more races.  12.54% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,813 households out of which 30.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 49.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 34.4% are non-families. 30.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.49 and the average family size is 3.04.

In the city the population is spread out with 25.4% under the age of 18, 10.9% from 18 to 24, 27.4% from 25 to 44, 18.6% from 45 to 64, and 17.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.7 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $28,557, and the median income for a family is $33,927. Males have a median income of $26,315 versus $19,442 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,281.  19.2% of the population and 12.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 23.5% of those under the age of 18 and 13.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

Carthage has one [[Carthage Senior High School (Missouri)|high school]], one junior high school, and five elementary schools.

==Culture==
Carthage was the site of the [[Battle of Carthage (1861)|Battle of Carthage]], an early skirmish in the [[American Civil War]], on July 5, 1861.  Local groups stage [http://www.geocities.com/battleofcarthage/ reenactments] of the battle, near the grounds of the [http://www.mostateparks.com/carthage.htm State Historic Site] which commemorates the event.

Since [[1978]], Carthage has hosted the annual [[Marian Days]] celebration for [[Vietnamese American]] [[Roman Catholic Church|Catholics]].  The event, which typically draws 50,000 to 70,000 attendees, takes place on the 28-acre campus of the Congregation of the Mother Co-Redemptrix, a Vietnamese order of priests and brothers which came from [[Vietnam]] to settle in Carthage in [[1975]], immediately following the [[Vietnam War]].[http://ncronline.org/NCR_Online/archives2/2004c/092404/092404j.php]

Carthage is also the home of the [[Precious Moments]] Chapel, a tourist attraction with paintings of the popular porcelain figurines.[http://www.preciousmoments.com/park/attractions/]

Carthage is located on Historic [[Route 66]].

== Notable natives ==
*[[A. P. (Ace) Borger]], businessman associated with Texas (1888-1934)
*[[Jann Carl]], ''[[Entertainment Tonight]]'' correspondent (b. 1960)
*[[Karl Hackett]], actor in numerous Westerns in the 1930s and 1940s (1893-1948)
*[[Carl Hubbell]], baseball player (1903-1988)
*[[Marlin Perkins]], naturalist and host of ''Mutual of Omaha's [[Wild Kingdom]]'' (1905-1986)
*[[Belle Starr]] (Myra MayBelle Shirley), Wild West outlaw (1848-1889)

== External links ==
*[http://www.visit-carthage.com/ &lt;nowiki&gt;Carthage, Missouri Convention &amp; Visitors Bureau&lt;/nowiki&gt;]

{{Mapit-US-cityscale|37.167773|-94.314958}}

