      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Jasper''' is a city located in [[Jasper County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,011.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Jasper.png|right|Location of Jasper, Missouri]]

Jasper is located at 37&amp;deg;20'8&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;18'1&quot; West (37.335679, -94.300174){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.8 km&amp;sup2; (1.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.79% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,011 people, 409 households, and 271 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 354.9/km&amp;sup2; (921.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 454 housing units at an average density of 159.4/km&amp;sup2; (413.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 95.85% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.30% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.89% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.20% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.40% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.37% from two or more races.  2.57% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 409 households out of which 31.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 51.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 33.7% are non-families. 30.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.45 and the average family size is 3.01.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.3% under the age of 18, 9.2% from 18 to 24, 23.4% from 25 to 44, 22.0% from 45 to 64, and 17.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 86.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.9 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $27,650, and the median income for a family is $31,667. Males have a median income of $26,304 versus $19,219 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,067.  12.4% of the population and 10.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 17.2% of those under the age of 18 and 9.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.


== Jasper in Media ==
Jasper is the setting of the 1989 movie [[Road_House_%281989_film%29|Road House]], starring [[Patrick Swayze]]; however, the movie was not actually filmed in Jasper and bears little resemblance to the town in geography or nature.

