      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Sarcoxie''' is a city located in [[Jasper County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,354.

== History ==
The earliest settler is said to be Chief Sarcoxie. His name has been said to mean &quot;As Tall As He Is&quot; which is a reference to his position and perhaps also his actual heighth. As a town settlement began in the 1830s with the town being platted in 1840. It is the only town in the US with the name Sarcoxie and is also the oldest town in the county.

The town was a minor flashpoint in the US Civil War with a Confederate flag flying in town for a time. In [[1887]] it became perhaps the first town in southwest Missouri to have electric lighting. 

Currently the town is noted for a craft mall and gazebo. The nearby caves also have the &quot;Ozark Cave Fish&quot;, an endemic species to the area.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Sarcoxie.png|right|Location of Sarcoxie, Missouri]]

Sarcoxie is located at 37&amp;deg;4'7&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;7'21&quot; West (37.068490, -94.122450){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.8 km&amp;sup2; (1.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,354 people, 559 households, and 359 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 484.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,254.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 635 housing units at an average density of 227.0/km&amp;sup2; (588.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 95.94% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.07% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.96% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.07% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.95% from two or more races.  0.81% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 559 households out of which 31.1% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 50.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.6% are non-families. 32.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 19.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.36 and the average family size is 2.99.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.4% under the age of 18, 7.9% from 18 to 24, 25.5% from 25 to 44, 19.3% from 45 to 64, and 20.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 80.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 75.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $25,000, and the median income for a family is $34,519. Males have a median income of $26,250 versus $20,547 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $13,531.  16.8% of the population and 10.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 21.3% of those under the age of 18 and 18.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Notable natives ==
*[[G. Lloyd Spencer]]-US Senator for Arkansas.

