      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Festus''' is a city located in [[Jefferson County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 9,660. Festus is the hometown of the Bottle Rockets, a noted alternative rock band who were recently named in an online poll &quot;The Best Bar Band in America&quot;.

Festus is often referred to in association with its neighbor, [[Crystal City, Missouri]], as the &quot;Twin Cities&quot;; however, the cities are incorporated separately.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Festus.png|right|Location of Festus, Missouri]]

Festus is located at 38&amp;deg;13'10&quot; North, 90&amp;deg;24'3&quot; West (38.219490, -90.400936){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 12.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  12.4 km&amp;sup2; (4.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 9,660 people, 3,861 households, and 2,606 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 780.3/km&amp;sup2; (2,020.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 4,040 housing units at an average density of 326.3/km&amp;sup2; (844.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 93.66% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.93% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.30% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.72% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.37% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.96% from two or more races.  1.04% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 3,861 households out of which 33.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 49.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.5% are non-families. 28.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 12.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.45 and the average family size is 2.97.

In the city the population is spread out with 25.8% under the age of 18, 9.5% from 18 to 24, 28.3% from 25 to 44, 20.5% from 45 to 64, and 15.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.6 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $36,687, and the median income for a family is $46,940. Males have a median income of $36,159 versus $25,108 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $19,035.  10.2% of the population and 7.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 13.6% of those under the age of 18 and 6.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

