      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Holden''' is a city located in [[Johnson County, Missouri]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,510.

== Geography ==
[[Image:MOMap-doton-Holden.png|right|Location of Holden, Missouri]]

Holden is located at 38&amp;deg;42'52&quot; North, 93&amp;deg;59'26&quot; West (38.714455, -93.990513){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 6.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.2 km&amp;sup2; (2.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.41% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,510 people, 990 households, and 656 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 402.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,040.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,089 housing units at an average density of 174.5/km&amp;sup2; (451.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 94.50% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.91% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 1.08% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.12% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.16% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.19% from two or more races.  1.08% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 990 households out of which 36.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 33.7% are non-families. 29.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.53 and the average family size is 3.11.

In the city the population is spread out with 30.0% under the age of 18, 11.0% from 18 to 24, 28.0% from 25 to 44, 17.3% from 45 to 64, and 13.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 96.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.7 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $30,255, and the median income for a family is $35,234. Males have a median income of $26,285 versus $20,884 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $13,537.  12.5% of the population and 10.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 11.4% of those under the age of 18 and 23.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== City Government ==

Mayor:  Terry Hedglin

== Neighboring Towns and Communities ==

